uisite.<br /> <br /> The only things in the extended Begotten template that require Family Ties concern themselves with either the ability to develop a new power or the ongoing ability to pass casual scrutiny as the same sort of monster, and Atavisms exist at the opposite end of the Satiety scale from where those powers are relevant to the natural trajectory of its resident Beast; relying on the overtly shocking power of Atavisms generally means opportunities for Kinship are more fraught and isolating.*<br /> <br /> A Merit to boost an Atavism should therefore lean on more permanent elements of the character or their Hunger. For example:<br /> <br /> <b>Child of the Dark (\u2022-\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Prerequisite:</b> Survival dots equal to rating.<br /> Your Horror is practically synonymous with a particular aspect of its Lair, and more readily exerts its power in such places.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> When you take this Merit, choose a Lair Trait and an Atavism. When in the presence of that Lair Trait, you may add your dots in this Merit to 3 for the purposes of permitting the use of the linked Atavism's Low Satiety effect. This Merit may be purchased multiple times, with each purchase reflecting a different Atavism; connecting a different Atavism to the same Lair Trait applies the full rating of the Merit associated with that Lair Trait to the new Atavism for the cost of one Merit dot. You may connect the same Atavism to different Lair Traits, but doing so adds two dots to the Merit cost.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Using the presence of one of your Lair Traits to apply another to a location costs an additional dot of Willpower if the linked Trait is not one of the Traits you are applying. Subtract your dots in this Merit from rolls to open a Primordial Pathway to a place without the linked Lair Trait. Subtract your dots in this Merit from your Lair rating for the purposes of determining how many times per scene you may use the presence of a Lair Trait to use the linked Atavism's Satiety Expenditure effect by spending Willpower instead of Satiety for any Lair Trait other than the linked Trait.<br /> <br /> <b>Riddling Presence (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Trained Observer 3, We Know All Your Secrets<br /> Your time among keen-eyed and sharp-eared monsters has stirred dormant aspects of your Horror to better leverage its senses.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Once per chapter, when your character uses an Atavism effect that provides them with knowledge or sensory information about a person in your presence (such as Needs Must, Mimir's Wisdom, or some applications of Shadowed Soul or Heart of the Ocean) you may spend a point of Willpower and roll Presence + Intelligence + Lair to treat them as a Contact in a relevant sphere of your choice for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Home Ground (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Prerequisites:</b> You Cannot Kill It, Occult 3<br /> Your time among hardy and resilient monsters has given you insight into their persistence that grants you a conditional form of their invulnerability.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> While in the presence of one of your Lair Traits or in the location of one of your Chambers, your character gains all the benefits of the Relentless Hunter and Unbreakable Atavisms even if they do not have it. If they do have that Atavism, they recover a point of Willpower at the end of any scene in which they use their Satiety Expenditure effects.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> When you take this Merit, choose three Lair Traits you do not have. The presence of any of those Lair Traits prevents you from gaining the benefits of the Relentless Hunter or Unbreakable Atavisms even if you have them normally.<br /> <br /> * Tangentially related, a weird side avenue:<br /> <br /> <b>Storied Advocate (\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Prerequisites:</b> Fame (Advanced), Any Kinship Nightmare<br /> You use your place in the collective unconscious as a means to more comprehensively spread fear of particular monsters.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You may apply your Advanced Fame dots as a bonus to any Nightmare that you can reasonably connect to a character who has the Family Ties Condition tagged to your character. In addition, you may use a Kinship Nightmare you do not know on a human character once per chapter as long as it can be reasonably derived from a character who has the Family Ties Condition for you.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Characters who have the Family Ties Condition for your character suffer the drawback of a Fame Merit equal to your character's Advanced Fame dots during any story in which you use this Merit.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> I like these a lot! One question, though. Shouldn't Child Of The Dark subtract its rating from your current Satiety when in the presence of an appropriate Lair Trait, rather than add its rating?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T14:05:37-07:00","id":1132795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1122221#post1122221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first thing that comes to mind is that I don't feel Family Ties are an appropriate prerequisite for Merits. These aren't like Werewolf's Code of Honor, where the associated Trait can change but naturally justifies itself toward one end of the scale over the other with sufficient instability; Conditions can be long-lasting or even nigh-on permanent, but their relation to Merits doesn't work in that direction and it especially doesn't work that way when Family Ties is a Condition that <i>other characters</i> have \u2014 if Display of Might remains an element of your character after the Titan changes Refinements or reaches the New Dawn or perishes or severs ties with you, then there is no mechanical point to the prerequisite.<br /> <br /> The only things in the extended Begotten template that require Family Ties concern themselves with either the ability to develop a new power or the ongoing ability to pass casual scrutiny as the same sort of monster, and Atavisms exist at the opposite end of the Satiety scale from where those powers are relevant to the natural trajectory of its resident Beast; relying on the overtly shocking power of Atavisms generally means opportunities for Kinship are more fraught and isolating.*<br /> <br /> A Merit to boost an Atavism should therefore lean on more permanent elements of the character or their Hunger. For example:<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I see where you are coming from, but I feel that, since Kinship Nightmares are a Thing, this should be acceptable. Basically, it is learning something about your Cousins that is similar to yourself (the preexisting Atavism), and expending the effort to acquire it for yourself to an extent. Acquiring it presumes a close relationship of some sort, just like how I can acquire an exclusive Fighting Style or Discipline or Gift from a mentor. In short, the Horror tries not to just pass as one of them, but tries to BE like one (building and expanding on a pre-existing mechanic). As such, the Kinship is a requirement for the purchase, NOT for keeping the Merit. And since the Horror is a malleable dreamform that can explicitly be impacted by e.g. Broodmates' lair traits and abilities (the fluffy reason for getting Heart of the Ocean for your Troll after joining a Brood with a Makara and Suffocating), I see no problem with that from a narrative/fluff standpoint. But then again, every table is different.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T17:14:07-07:00","id":1132847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1132649#post1132649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I like these a lot! One question, though. Shouldn't Child Of The Dark subtract its rating from your current Satiety when in the presence of an appropriate Lair Trait, rather than add its rating?</div> </div> </div> </div>It raises the upper Satiety limit at which you can use the Low Satiety effect (e.g. at two dots you can use the effect at Satiety 5), but yeah, &quot;treat your current Satiety as though it were [dots] lower for the purposes of Low Satiety Atavism effects&quot; also tracks; as-written the Merit is kind of thrown together, but on a subsequent draft I'd probably be figuring out which particular framing to go with and tweaking the drawback to better suit that choice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1132795#post1132795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see where you are coming from, but I feel that, since Kinship Nightmares are a Thing, this should be acceptable.</div> </div> </div> </div>My entire premise here is that the Kinship is just the temporary connection rather than the long-term change to your supernatural makeup that purchasing a Nightmare or otherwise modifying the character represents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-22-2017, 08:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T18:06:23-07:00","id":1132868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1132847#post1132847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My entire premise here is that the Kinship is just the temporary connection rather than the long-term change to your supernatural makeup that purchasing a Nightmare or otherwise modifying the character represents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I don't quite follow: establishing Kinship and using that as grounds to purchase a Nightmare (thus modyfing the supernatural makeup of the character) is okay, but not ok for merits? Is that what you mean?<br /> <br /> If you mean &quot;Why make it a requirement in the first place if you can keep the ability even when the Kinship ends?&quot;, my answer is simply: because it is more interesting, it provides a different kind of expression for the character, and having it end would be perfectly fine with me too, honestly. (Sanctity of Merits is a thing, so this would be narratively interesting without mechanically disadvantaging the player).<br /> <br /> If my response does not really follow up to what you say: Sorry! In my defense, it is late and I have been working on my theses for 15 hours now. Not quite functional for non-thesis things atm I am afraid. Unless you'd want to talk about dragons, that I can do right now due to thesis.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T21:51:57-07:00","id":1132914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1132868#post1132868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I don't quite follow: establishing Kinship and using that as grounds to purchase a Nightmare (thus modyfing the supernatural makeup of the character) is okay, but not ok for merits? Is that what you mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Merits generally have stable prerequisites that often factor into their continued usability \u2014 Area of Expertise becomes completely useless if you lose the Skill that makes it work, but it takes extraordinary circumstances to lose Skill dots in general \u2014 whereas Kinship Nightmares have a gateway circumstance that can be completely unintentional but serves to let the character grow their supernatural power in a sort of digestive manner \u2014 once you've internalized the fear of an implacable enemy that your Promethean sister represents by learning You Cannot Kill It, that Nightmare stays learned, and the only prerequisite to its usability is that you have any Satiety at all.<br /> <br /> Applying Family Ties serves a similar function to having Connected, in that it represents a bond that goes away when bridges are burned or one party no longer exists, but Connected is not a prerequisite for having a given Social Merit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you mean &quot;Why make it a requirement in the first place if you can keep the ability even when the Kinship ends?&quot;, my answer is simply: because it is more interesting, it provides a different kind of expression for the character, and having it end would be perfectly fine with me too, honestly. (Sanctity of Merits is a thing, so this would be narratively interesting without mechanically disadvantaging the player). </div> </div> </div>One of the principal tensions in Beast is that your Kinship with other monsters only really gives you connections with individual monsters for as long as that connection isn't severed, and there are legitimate reasons for characters (your own or others) to want to sever that connection; powerful Beasts who want to maintain a Kinship with a particular type of monster despite the notional obligations of family and the reduced feeding pool and the pressures of low Satiety to hurt the monsters closest to them often wind up isolating and/or consuming their charges.<br /> <br /> If there were to be a consistent prerequisite for a Beast Merit based on a Kinship, I feel that a more coherent choice would be having a Social Merit tagged to a given monster or group of monsters, or having knowledge of a particular Kinship Nightmare like I did above; Family Ties has the awkward distinction of not just being a Condition, but being a Condition <i>that another character has</i>, which itself makes having it as a dependent prerequisite for a Merit's use by the Beast serve as an abandonment-detector in a way that doesn't track too well.<br /> <br /> You could make a Merit whose effect depends on having a given active Kinship, maybe, but that seems more in the vein of a variable Merit than a set of specific bonuses. For instance:<br /> <br /> <b>Your Mother's Eye (\u2022-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Beast, Occult or Socialize 2<br /> You mirror the abilities of your kin at a more inconstant level than the slow adaptation of your Horror.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> At the start of any chapter, you may distribute your dots in this Merit between any Merits or Skill rating possessed by a character who is related to your character by blood or who has the Family Ties Condition tagged to your character; borrowing a Skill that you do not possess any dots in costs a point of Willpower per roll, but having dots in a Skill reduces the dot cost of benefiting from your kin's rating to the difference between the two (i.e. if you have three dots in this Merit and two dots of Socialize, borrowing your mother's three dots of Socialize would only take one of your three dots in this Merit).<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> At the end of any chapter in which you benefit from the effects of this Merit, roll your Lair rating. On a success, lose one point of Satiety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T05:24:14-07:00","id":1132974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1132914#post1132914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Merits generally have stable prerequisites that often factor into their continued usability \u2014 Area of Expertise becomes completely useless if you lose the Skill that makes it work, but it takes extraordinary circumstances to lose Skill dots in general \u2014 whereas Kinship Nightmares have a gateway circumstance that can be completely unintentional but serves to let the character grow their supernatural power in a sort of digestive manner \u2014 once you've internalized the fear of an implacable enemy that your Promethean sister represents by learning You Cannot Kill It, that Nightmare stays learned, and the only prerequisite to its usability is that you have any Satiety at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well - yeah? Generally being the case does not mean that exceptions to the rule are not possible. I also do not see why merits, which are not necessarily a stable, permanent thing, should exlusively have permanent prerequisites, after all <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Merits often represent things that can go away. Retainers can be killed. Mentors can get impatient and stop dispensing wisdom. So while Merits may represent temporary facets of your character, Merit points continue to exist. At the end of any chapter where your character has lost Merits, you can replace them with another Merit. </div> </div> </div>. To repeat: it is a learning requirement to gain access to those merits, not a requirement to use them.<br /> <br /> Maybe this is more of a hack to you, but a Kinship-based system that does for Atavisms a bit of what Kinship does for Nightmares is something I personally would just do with something like Merits, since there should be some sort of xp-cost to it. I would like to make more use of Kinship in my games, and just 'fitting in' is not always enough to translate this sense of Beast's Family. If a Beast can internalize what makes another scary, and express that via Nightmares, I personally feel it is fine to also take note of similarities, internalizen the small but decisive differences, and express them via the Horror. I see where you are coming from, don't get me wrong, but I don't think this approach is entirely wrong. Yes, it is strange, and kind of unusual, but so are Beasts.<br /> <br /> But okay, let's just call this a hack: If I would just change the name of the mechanic from Merits to something else - oh I don't know, Evolutions? - and propose that to acquire an Evolution, one must have an Atavism and a Kinship, that'd be fine, right?<br /> <br /> You got me thinking, though: I also could just take those Merits above, and make them conditions, instead. Conditions with prerequisites and very powerful benefits, so I'd want to put on some harsh additional requirements. But sure, that might work. Hm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1132914#post1132914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Applying Family Ties serves a similar function to having Connected, in that it represents a bond that goes away when bridges are burned or one party no longer exists, but Connected is not a prerequisite for having a given Social Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>We do, however, have K-9 and Falconry, Fighting Styles that have the Bonded Condition as a prerequisite. So it is not like there is no precedent for Conditions as a prerequisite. Plus the above aren't exactly Social Merits.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: I do like Your Mother's Eye!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 08-23-2017, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T12:41:01-07:00","id":1133117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1132974#post1132974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We do, however, have K-9 and Falconry, Fighting Styles that have the Bonded Condition as a prerequisite. So it is not like there is no precedent for Conditions as a prerequisite. Plus the above aren't exactly Social Merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>That there is a certain redundancy written in the formatting of those Merits that happens to span into the Prerequisites section doesn't really change the fact that &quot;This Merit works on any animal of the appropriate type that you share the Bonded Condition with and have had an appropriate amount of time to train&quot; is closer to &quot;This Merit works with these types of weapon and doesn't work without one of them&quot; than &quot;You can't practically have this Merit without currently having an instance of this Condition.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe this is more of a hack to you, but a Kinship-based system that does for Atavisms a bit of what Kinship does for Nightmares is something I personally would just do with something like Merits, since there should be some sort of xp-cost to it. I would like to make more use of Kinship in my games, and just 'fitting in' is not always enough to translate this sense of Beast's Family. </div> </div> </div>You could also make a Merit that modifies Passing Resemblance or Family Dinner or lets you &quot;save&quot; a number of Kinship bonds based on Lair; there's a number of potential workarounds to the thing, but the main dichotomy I keep going back to is that Atavisms are very direct and incontrovertible expressions of the Begotten nature through lasting adaptations of the Horror, and that this contrasts against Kinship's greater focus on letting your environment do your job for you by empowering monstrous proxies or bringing the broader framework of Nightmares to bear on a subject or drawing your Chambers to more loosely-related areas and blending into the background as a mundane human or a different sort of monster.<br /> <br /> Accordingly, I feel like changes to Atavisms that are related to Kinship in a sense more involved than narrative justification for buying a new Atavism should either filter those relationships through the Hunger-weighted side of the scale or bring more of the complications of Kinship to the use of the Atavism \u2014 if you're binding one of the truest expressions of your power to an external source, you should either have a greater incentive to internalize that source (maybe take the Addicted Condition tied to their presence or some shared ritual between the pair of you) or become more susceptible to that source's influence (e.g. take a Persistent form of Swooning for the source of the Merit).<br /> <br /> Outside the context of learning Nightmares, Kinships key into a whole narrative framework of support and vulnerability that doesn't quite mesh with a straightforward &quot;buff the powers that mark me as specifically a Beast&quot; trick \u2014 even within the context of Kinship Nightmares, exhibiting an uncommon power implies a referent from which the Begotten developed that ability, which suggests either the relationship still exists or something happened to it that hints at the power of the Beast or the existence of something stronger than them that they no longer keep in touch with; &quot;I learned this from my time in Boston courting an unkillable terror&quot; is still a story to tell even if you killed that terror or parted with them on unfriendly terms or never remember to write home and ask about their kids, and that relationship doesn't call for the same upkeep as befriending a walking forest to disguise yourself as a tree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You got me thinking, though: I also could just take those Merits above, and make them conditions, instead. Conditions with prerequisites and very powerful benefits, so I'd want to put on some harsh additional requirements. But sure, that might work. Hm. </div> </div> </div>Speaking as someone who's got at least two PCs with semi-unique bits of potent supernatural weirdness going on represented as Persistent Conditions, I would heartily endorse this method.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T14:04:10-07:00","id":1133155,"title":"","content":"Family Ties can be a prerequisite for Merits. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (You'll have to wait to see why)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T09:32:05-07:00","id":1135813,"title":"","content":"I was reading through Dark Eras and came on text that describes an Egg taken from what looks like beasts layer and into the real world. page 293. Any thoughts on that? Like did that beast had some unique merit, was it an atavism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T09:34:00-07:00","id":1135814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1135813#post1135813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was reading through Dark Eras and came on text that describes an Egg taken from what looks like beasts layer and into the real world. page 293. Any thoughts on that? Like did that beast had some unique merit, was it an atavism?</div> </div> </div> </div>I did make an Ugallu Atavism that involves resurrecting via hatching from an egg created in the Lair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T12:34:32-07:00","id":1135874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1135814#post1135814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did make an Ugallu Atavism that involves resurrecting via hatching from an egg created in the Lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHm. interesting. So those hunters stole the Save egg and were going to sell it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T14:50:33-07:00","id":1135939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1135874#post1135874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bHm. interesting. So those hunters stole the Save egg and were going to sell it?</div> </div> </div> </div>More likely it was the Beast's broodmate who had yet to hatch/reincarnate from a previous death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T22:59:57-07:00","id":1138511,"title":"","content":"<b>Conjoined Horror:</b> (ooo to ooooo)<br /> <br /> You did not go through your devouring alone, you have one or more identical siblings who all fell victim to the same Horror simultaneously. Now, your souls are merged as one, taking the form of a great, multi-headed Beast.<br /> <br /> <b>Effects:</b> Your character is part of a set of identical siblings who are all in sync with one another. Not only do they look identical, but they think and act identically, as well. Mechanically, this gives the player access to multiple copies of the same character, allowing them to exist in multiple locations in the physical world at the same time. While the siblings share each other's skills and attributes, they do not automatically share knowledge, unless they have another merit / ability which enables them to do so.<br /> <br /> This merit can only be taken at character creation, and if one of the siblings should happen to die, they permanently lose the benefits of their respective rank in this merit.<br /> <br /> The 3rd dot version of this merit results in identical twins, the fourth dot produces identical triplets, and the fifth dot results in identical quadruplets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T18:50:00-07:00","id":1138774,"title":"","content":"<b>Dark Denizens (\u2022-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Beast<br /> Your Lair is not limited to illusory habitants. You have developed an ecosystem capable of sustaining a number of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream\"><b>Night Terrors.</b></a><br /> <b>Effect:</b> For every dot in this Merit, each Chamber in your Lair has 3 dots worth of Rank for Night Terrors. You may choose to have fewer instances with higher Rank, or more instances with lower Rank. Since they are most comfortable in a Chamber that suits their Hunger, they will usually stay there. However, you may force all your Night Terrors to go into the same Chamber by spending 1 Satiety. This lasts for one scene and can be done a number of times per Story equal to [highest between your rating in this Merit and Lair].<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Even the most loyal of Night Terrors will turn against their masters if not properly fed. They require a number of Satiety points every week equal to [dot rating in this Merit] to remain satisfied. This can either be given by the Beast through an act similar to Mother's Kiss, or come from anyone who happens to find their way into the Lair. Should they not receive this, they will escape the Lair like a Horror going Rampant and Feed on people in the material world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 09-15-2017, 12:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T15:39:45-07:00","id":1144988,"title":"","content":"<b>Gigantic Weapons (o-ooooo; Style)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Strength &gt;5 OR Cyclopean Strength<br /> Others might use swords and hammers, but your ability and strength are heightened to a degree that you can successfuly use weapons other People wouldn't even be able to lift. The weapon has to have markings of classic weaponry - oversized Buster Swords, gigantic Shaolin Spears, proper Clubs etc. qualify, car-doors (or cars) and other improvised weaponry does not.<br /> <b>o </b>When using an overdimensioned weapon, you gain Reach.<br /> <b>oo</b> Substracts the Targets Stamina by the weapons size/2 rounded up to determine effects like knocked down/stunned....<br /> <b>ooo </b>It's not the edge that kills, but the pure force of the impact: sacrifice your defense to ignore (Dots in this style/2 rounded up) Armor for your next attack<br /> <b>oooo </b>Making use of the huge size of your weapon in wide Arcs, you can sacrifice your defence for a turn to attack several opponents, as Long as they are within Reach<br /> <b>ooooo</b> You can make an All-Out-Attack and Combine it with any of the manouveurs in this style.<br /> <br /> Alternatively for <b>oo</b>: When attacking another armed fighter, disarm then upon dealing dealing damage higher than their Weaponry. (Especially nice for some dark eras?)<br /> Comments?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T15:55:14-07:00","id":1144994,"title":"","content":"Fifth dot doesn't work with third or fourth. You generally can't mix different defence removing manoeuvres, and if you remove that restriction you have absolutely no reason not to constantly use it with 3 and 4 since you've already lost all defence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T16:09:17-07:00","id":1144997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1144994#post1144994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fifth dot doesn't work with third or fourth. You generally can't mix different defence removing manoeuvres, and if you remove that restriction you have absolutely no reason not to constantly use it with 3 and 4 since you've already lost all defence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fifth dot basically is meant to turn the &quot;sacrifice defense&quot; requirement into &quot;make an all-out attack&quot; - you still sacrifice defense, but also gain some dice. We already have some styles that require you to make an all out attack to benefit from the style's move (e.g. relentless assault or brute force), which is why I thought this is fair game.<br /> <br /> So yeah, it is meant as a passive buff and meant to be always used with 3 or 4. Think it's too strong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T16:18:12-07:00","id":1145000,"title":"","content":"Not too strong. Mostly it's just that I don't like that rule about multiple sacrifices of defense being ignored, even if official Merits also does it, and that it's boring that the fifth dot in a Style is a simple dice modifier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T16:49:41-07:00","id":1145010,"title":"","content":"ooooo- when making an attack with an oversized weapon, spent a wp to sent your target flying: they are pushed back 10 metres and unless they succeded on a dext+ath dice roll, they are also knocked down. Should this send them against a wall, they Suffer an additional 2 bashing and are stunned for a turn.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> how about that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T07:45:24-08:00","id":1185172,"title":"","content":"Working on &quot;Family Fighting Styles&quot; (just for fun), based on the Families' main characteristics and Birthrights. I'd like some feedback on the general concepts, this is all very early and basically off the top of my head. But since I love Martial Arts and Beast, I'd like to combine the two (maybe for a Dark Era game. Both Three Kingdoms of Darkness and Fallen Blossoms come to mind as near-ideal settings). Many of these ideas seem stronger than normal styles, which is why I think there'd be higher/additional requirements (certain advanced merits, for example).<br /> <br /> Imo, Makara should feature a grappling fighting style - fits with the themes of taking someone out of their depths, chokeholds resemble the Birthright, and punching and being underwater don't mesh well, which is a main association with the Family. So a style adding special maneuvers like joint locks and choke holds, maybe allow them to grapple multiple opponents at once.<br /> <br /> Ugallu seem the Ueshiba kind to me: relaxed, hard to hit, don't strike often but always hard, not necessarily faster but always in the right spot to intercept/evade/counterattack, as if they <i>knew </i>you'd try that. After all, their fluff is all about seeing through people, so let's cram this up to Sharingan-levels here =P Stuff like keeping defense against multiple opponents, applying defense against firearms/projectile weapons they are aware of, debuff-inflicting strikes to the head/eyes to neutralize a target...<br /> <br /> Namtaru are disgusting, but to me, their most striking physical aspect is outlasting the opponent: in-Family Atavisms like Infestation and Unbreakable make it harder to be killed, Shadowed Soul helps avoid being attacked altogether and Basilisk's Touch is not the weapon of someone that tries to one-hit-K.O. someone. So maybe a Bonus to Defense, Going-all-out granting temporary armor, and debuff-inflicting attacks. I thought what might be an appropriate five-dot skills is the following: After taking a Weaponry hit, the Beast may op to take Bonus damage and a Debuff themselves (like Arm-wreck) to represent a shocking display of defiance and disarm the opponent (block a knife by going full-anime and grapping the hand after the blade has pierced the hand or use a headbutt to the shaft to blow a hammer strike away). In addition to being disarmed, the opponent might have to roll resolve+composure to not freak out, take a Tilt like &quot;Sick&quot; or a penalty to attacking the beast due to sheer freak-out.<br /> <br /> Eshmaki are definitly the ambush-type. Skills like additional damage on surprise attacks, spending WP to inflict a condition with a surprise attack, establishing a grapple in a surprise attack allows to follow up immediately with a grapple action as if rolling an exceptional success, spending WP to give a surprise attack the rote quality or similar all seem like a prime choice.<br /> <br /> Anakim are all about making you feel helpless. Very Going-All-Out based fighting style, Spending WP to subtract successes from a successfull attack and reduce the opponents defense pool for the rest of the fight/inflict arm wreck or similar conditions/ cause negative penalties. Spending WP to gain 8-again/have an attack apply to multiple opponents/turn Fists into +1Lethal weapons using a Strength+Brawl dicepool.<br /> <br /> <br /> Please feel free to comment, critizise, explain and point out what I missed/your point of view. All help welcome =)<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> Another idea for Ugallu: ignoring enemy defense for a WP.<br /> For Anakim: a bonus on grapple-ending actions (e.g. Grapple action Push or Throw)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 02-14-2018, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T16:12:46-08:00","id":1194081,"title":"","content":"Recently had this idea for a merit for Heroes, thought I'd post it here:<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Slayer's Insight (OO)<br /> \u200bPrerequisites: Hero, Must have slain 2 or more Beasts of select Family/Hunger</b><br /> A Hero's Legend becomes better at imposing itself on certain kinds of Beasts, at the expense of weakening against others. To the Hero though, it is simply that their experience fighting Beasts of a certain kind has allowed them to spot shared weakness or flaws in their enemy.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Effect</b>: Upon taking this merit, select a Beast Family or Hunger, when attempting to inflict Anathema on a Beast of that category, the Hero's rolls gain the 9-again quality.<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: When trying to inflict Anathema on Beasts outside that category, the Hero's rolls lose the 10-again quality<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bNote, I'm very foggy on mechanical details, so if someone thinks this should be altered, let me know.<br /> <br /> \u200b==Edit==<br /> <br /> \u200bI changed it from a Three dot to Two dot at the suggestion of Wormwood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":17107,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","user":"Mangaholic13","date":". 03-11-2018, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T00:28:35-08:00","id":1194164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangaholic13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1194081#post1194081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Recently had this idea for a merit for Heroes, thought I'd post it here:<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Slayer's Insight (OOO)<br /> \u200bPrerequisites: Hero, Must have slain 2 or more Beasts of select Family/Hunger</b><br /> A Hero's Legend becomes better at imposing itself on certain kinds of Beasts, at the expense of weakening against others. To the Hero though, it is simply that their experience fighting Beasts of a certain kind has allowed them to spot shared weakness or flaws in their enemy.<br /> <br /> \u200bEffect: Upon taking this merit, select a Beast Family or Hunger, when attempting to inflict Anathema on a Beast of that category, the Hero's rolls gain the 9-again quality.<br /> Drawback: When trying to inflict Anathema on Beasts outside that category, the Hero's rolls lose the 10-again quality<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bNote, I'm very foggy on mechanical details, so if someone thinks this should be altered, let me know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. I like that one. Somehow very obvious and yet didn't appear yet. I think you might want to bump the cost down to OO though or give it 8-again, since the drawback balances it out fairly well imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T00:36:44-08:00","id":1194166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1194164#post1194164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heh. I like that one. Somehow very obvious and yet didn't appear yet. I think you might want to bump the cost down to OO though or give it 8-again, since the drawback balances it out fairly well imo.</div> </div> </div> </div>I second that. It's a great idea - I love the idea of a Hero whose 'thing' is that he specifically hunts giants or sea monsters (why hello there, Ahab) - but having it at OOO with that Drawback is a little punishing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T14:35:45-07:00","id":1194368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1194164#post1194164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heh. I like that one. Somehow very obvious and yet didn't appear yet. I think you might want to bump the cost down to OO though or give it 8-again, since the drawback balances it out fairly well imo.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYeah, I was a little surprised that no one less had thought of it. I mean, Conquering Heroes introduced a Hero who exclusively goes after Makara. I'll modify it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T10:40:17-07:00","id":1195369,"title":"","content":"<b>Extra Lair Trait (\u2022\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> All Lairs are dangerous; yours is even more so. Gain an additional Lair Trait. The two-dot version of this Merit offers a Minor Trait, while the four-dot grants a Major one. This Merit does not increase the maximum number of Lair Traits you can impose in a scene.<br /> <br /> This is a simple Merit that I homebrewed for my own games, because I really like Lair Traits. I'm a little worried it might be breaching into &quot;no-brainer&quot; territory, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":".  Increased the dot rating 03-15-2018, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T01:58:13-07:00","id":1195660,"title":"","content":"I'd up the cost- Lair traits are very powerful, and having additional ones increase the likelihood of using them manyfold. Even one more minor trait gives you immunities that are eventual gamechangers. Major ones even more so.<br /> Think of it like this: an immunity to e.g. visual impairments, + the ability to cause it, + a circumstance in which you gain +1 die on rolls to open primordial pathways and, iirc, in which you can use sat expenditure effects of atavisms without spending the satiety.<br /> The only drawback is that it is circumstantial, but still. OOO and OOOO would be a better price imo.<br /> Otherwise yeah, this really should've been a no-brainer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T06:40:24-07:00","id":1195708,"title":"","content":"Yeah, maybe instead of just a straight up +1 Lair Trait, you make it more conditional? Like you don't get the normal immunity, or can't use the extra as a link for bringing in other Lair Traits, or something. Make it so the extra is Lair Trait-lite, so people have to decide if it is worth the XP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T06:55:31-07:00","id":1195711,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I mean, 4 xp is equal to an out-of-family Atavism or Attribute, so if I can't use the Major Lair trait to chain link with others it'd suck.<br /> On the other hand, Immunity to, say, Suffocation, is not bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T20:11:35-07:00","id":1195935,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> Good point. I sometimes forget about all the tangential benefits of Lair Traits outside of their deleterious effects. I increased the dot rating of the Merit by one, and also added an extra (maybe unnecessary) qualifying clause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T20:42:05-07:00","id":1195941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1195660#post1195660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd up the cost- Lair traits are very powerful, and having additional ones increase the likelihood of using them manyfold. Even one more minor trait gives you immunities that are eventual gamechangers. Major ones even more so.<br /> Think of it like this: an immunity to e.g. visual impairments, + the ability to cause it, + a circumstance in which you gain +1 die on rolls to open primordial pathways and, iirc, in which you can use sat expenditure effects of atavisms without spending the satiety.<br /> The only drawback is that it is circumstantial, but still. OOO and OOOO would be a better price imo.<br /> Otherwise yeah, this really should've been a no-brainer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps amusingly, I made this same observation <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1063120#post1063120\">a year ago today</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T05:58:32-07:00","id":1196026,"title":"","content":"Heh. That is indeed amusing.<br /> <br /> I am currently thinking on what other Kinship merits we could come up with, and I keep thinking that we have a distinct lack of Spirit and Mummy Kinship Merits. Any ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T07:24:06-07:00","id":1196044,"title":"","content":"How about Slasher Kinship?<br /> <br /> Or Kinship with one of the Corebook example Horrors?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T12:22:58-07:00","id":1196160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1196026#post1196026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh. That is indeed amusing.<br /> <br /> I am currently thinking on what other Kinship merits we could come up with, and I keep thinking that we have a distinct lack of Spirit and Mummy Kinship Merits. Any ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking recently that a mummy Kinship Merit could let a Beast do something similar to kepher, or maybe use Relics without activating their curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T12:35:49-07:00","id":1196170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1196160#post1196160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking recently that a mummy Kinship Merit could let a Beast do something similar to kepher, or maybe use Relics without activating their curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they can 'appease' the curse with Satiety for a reasonable period of time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T12:45:42-07:00","id":1196177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1196044#post1196044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about Slasher Kinship?<br /> <br /> Or Kinship with one of the Corebook example Horrors?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHow about a Merit that lets a Beast, who has kinship with a Slasher, temporarily hide from Hero's Beast senses; based on how some monsters manage to hide from the hero in plain sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T13:28:54-07:00","id":1196202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangaholic13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1196177#post1196177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bHow about a Merit that lets a Beast, who has kinship with a Slasher, temporarily hide from Hero's Beast senses; based on how some monsters manage to hide from the hero in plain sight.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd make that very expensive or situational","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T13:53:16-07:00","id":1196217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1196044#post1196044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about Slasher Kinship?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Beast is instinctively aware of locations where someone lost Integrity and how that happened if that's the result of a Slasher killing someone there in the past. Easy Chambers on Elm Street, basically.<br /> <br /> I'm more wary of adding the chance to make a Chamber in such location regardless if it shares a Trait with the Beast's Lair, but it would be thematic and allow the Beast to make the sort of sudden apparitions movie Slashers do. Bending rules that way would make for an expensive Merit though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 03-16-2018, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T19:18:01-07:00","id":1196317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1196202#post1196202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd make that very expensive or situational</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell of course it would be either of those. Otherwise, it would break the game entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T15:59:53-07:00","id":1198438,"title":"","content":"A lot of these are really cool and nicely balanced, but I have to comment on one merit specifically:<br /> <br /> Ancient Horror is so incredibly powerful in its current form that, if allowed in-game, it would be a must-have on a scale that surpasses even Terrible Form from Demon or Driven from Promethean.<br /> <br /> Beasts are incredibly heavily incentivized to raise their Lair rating in large part because of the extra bonus it provides to Atavisms (though the in-built benefits of gaining extra Lair Traits etc is also incredibly valuable). <br /> <br /> Providing an effective 5 point increase in this usage of the Power stat for the cost of a single point is too good to pass up. If the group is using the Satiety-for-Beats implementation of hunger, then half of the downside becomes strictly an upside, too. The bonus could be cut down to half of your dots in he merit rounded down and it would <b>still</b> be extremely good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T16:40:25-07:00","id":1200257,"title":"","content":"An idea I had:<br /> <br /> <b>Escape Clause (</b><b>\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> When a Beast takes this Merit, the player designs an Escape Clause that ties into their character's Legend and Hunger. This is some action a person can take that renders them immune to feeding (for a time, at least). Returning the slab, showing the video tape to someone else, spreading goat's blood on one's front door, and apologizing sincerely are all examples of an Escape Clause. If a potential victim fulfills the requirements, the Beast can gain no Satiety from that person for the reset of the story, and also takes a Beat. To even harm said person requires spending a point of Willpower, and the roll is still penalized by the Beast's Satiety. Conversely, if the Beast does feed from someone who fails to fulfill the Escape Clause within the set parameters, increase the Satiety Potential of the meal by one.<br /> <br /> An Escape Clause in effect helps to solidify the narrative of a Beast. They are most often used by Nemeses, as a way out of suffering punishment, but any Hunger can find creative ways to use one, such as a Ravager that won't destroy a building marked with a certain arcane sigil, a Tyrant who respectfully withdraws from anyone who bests her in honorable combat, or a Predator who finds himself unable to kill anyone who's recently confessed their sins to a Catholic priest. An Escape Clause should be an action that an average person should have at least a chance to accomplish, though it does not have to be readily obvious or lacking in twists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T08:55:02-07:00","id":1200824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1200257#post1200257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To even harm said person requires spending a point of Willpower, and the roll is still penalized by the Beast's Satiety</div> </div> </div> </div>Could I suggest penalised by the distance of the Beast's Satiety from 5?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T09:11:22-07:00","id":1200833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1200257#post1200257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An idea I had:<br /> <br /> <b>Escape Clause (</b><b>\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> When a Beast takes this Merit, the player designs an Escape Clause that ties into their character's Legend and Hunger. This is some action a person can take that renders them immune to feeding (for a time, at least). Returning the slab, showing the video tape to someone else, spreading goat's blood on one's front door, and apologizing sincerely are all examples of an Escape Clause. If a potential victim fulfills the requirements, the Beast can gain no Satiety from that person for the reset of the story, and also takes a Beat. To even harm said person requires spending a point of Willpower, and the roll is still penalized by the Beast's Satiety. Conversely, if the Beast does feed from someone who fails to fulfill the Escape Clause within the set parameters, increase the Satiety Potential of the meal by one.<br /> <br /> An Escape Clause in effect helps to solidify the narrative of a Beast. They are most often used by Nemeses, as a way out of suffering punishment, but any Hunger can find creative ways to use one, such as a Ravager that won't destroy a building marked with a certain arcane sigil, a Tyrant who respectfully withdraws from anyone who bests her in honorable combat, or a Predator who finds himself unable to kill anyone who's recently confessed their sins to a Catholic priest. An Escape Clause should be an action that an average person should have at least a chance to accomplish, though it does not have to be readily obvious or lacking in twists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since this is basically a Ban, it seems more like an Anathema than a Merit a Beast would take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T11:35:31-07:00","id":1200901,"title":"","content":"I agree it's not much of a Merit, but conceptually it's too interesting to dismiss. Perhaps it could come with an additional benefit, like:<br /> <br /> 1. It's much more difficult to inflict an Anathema on the character, or the Anathemas are lessened in intensity. The Beast is creating their own Myth, which protects them against external influences.<br /> 2. A would be victim performing an Escape Clause grants the Beast a point of Satiety. The Horror doesn't get to feed <i>per se</i>, but as Goetia it's empowered by increased notoriety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T12:15:38-07:00","id":1200922,"title":"","content":"I'd make it, performing an Escape Clause <i>Intentionally, knowing there is a monster after them and this is how they stop them</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T05:23:32-07:00","id":1209984,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Mountain of Meat oooo</b></u><br /> Prerequisite: Giant, advanced<br /> <br /> The character isn't just towering, he's HUGE. Packed with muscles to the point even bodybuilders grow green with jealousy, the character enjoys a number of benefits:<br /> - muscle mass provides cushion: reduce bashing damage by 1.<br /> - although they are not actually taller, their effective Size is considered to be +1 for purposes of Health etc. due to the added musclemass<br /> - add 2 dice to Strength-related rolls<br /> <br /> However, being a towering bundle of meat has its drawbacks:<br /> - Consider Stamina to be at -1 for purposes of enduring hostile conditions, holding your breath, staying conscious etc. Basically, whenever it says (Stamina) Rounds, subtract one.<br /> - the body demands highly increased nourishment, and the character's wallet feels the effect: Resources is at -1. If the Character does not have the necessary financial means to provide for their needs, they have to steal, extort or otherwise acquire food IC or suffer from the Malnourished Condition.<br /> - looking inocuous is hard, and not drawing attention is even harder: people gain an additional +2 to remember or notice you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Malnourished</b></u> (Condition)<br /> <br /> The character severely lacks the necessary chemicals to keep themselves alive and their body functioning. Take a -3 to all physical actions. In addition, they cannot properly concentrate: mental skills lose the 10-again ability. Finally, looking intimidating is hard when you look sickly and weak - social rolls depending on physical strength or hostile authority also lose the 10-again ability. However, appealing to people's pity comes far easier when looking this pathetic: take 9-again on rolls appealing to people's empathy.<br /> <br /> Resolution: Eat appropriate foods and rest for (Size) hours afterwards.<br /> <br /> Beat: Fail at a task that would otherwise be easy because you are not in peak condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 04-22-2018, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T08:38:45-07:00","id":1210040,"title":"","content":"Maybe (Size) Hours?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T09:06:05-07:00","id":1210046,"title":"","content":"Actually, Hours makes more sense than turns. After all, turns are just a few seconds. I forgot about that for a bit. Consider it changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T15:11:45-07:00","id":1210166,"title":"","content":"Neat merit/condition combo! Although I think resolving it should take way longer.<br /> This should reflect a lifestyle, so the resolution should be closer to Size/2 days of constant nourishment (lack of rest could be factored in negatively) in my opinion. It could even take Size days, if the changes are so dramatic. &lt;normally I would go for an even longer period, but I think this is closer to what you feel comfortable with&gt;<br /> Of course this could be applied to the way you get the condition as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T15:22:29-07:00","id":1221557,"title":"","content":"The broad strokes of an idea: What rating and stipulations might be attached to an Awakened Kinship Merit that allows a character to form an Amnion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T00:03:23-07:00","id":1221623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1221557#post1221557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The broad strokes of an idea: What rating and stipulations might be attached to an Awakened Kinship Merit that allows a character to form an Amnion?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of Beasts being able to do more in the Anima Mundi, but I think that an Amnion may be the wrong way to go about it. An Amnion is an expression of individual will and self. What if a Beast's version is a strengthening of the 'myth' side of their Horror, the human-created side, to resist the primal side that is most close to the Dark Mother? Maybe entering it would require something like a watered-down Incarnation, or at least some mythological support in the 'real' world to maintain - you have to be a campfire story, so that that can feed you and maintain you in the face of the Ecstatic Winds.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Another option would be a Kinship with a Changing Breed (one of the shapeshifters with a nahual) that allows a Beast to take the form of their Horror in the Anima Mundi, using its shape and soul as a disguise to fool the Winds into thinking they're a native, or maybe some method of bringing their Lair with them as a shield.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 05-24-2018, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T02:40:22-07:00","id":1221638,"title":"","content":"Here's my attempt at a set of Amnion-style merits:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Humanity's Monster (O-OOOOO)</b></u><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Resolve 4, Silver Ladder Kinship <i>or</i> Mind 3 Mage Kinship<br /> <b>Effect:</b> To name something is to claim it. Infant Horrors squirm up out of the Mother's Land and are named and shaped by the Dark Dream of humanity. When the Beasts these Horrors bind to return to their Mother's Land, the Dark Mother attempts to embrace them once more - or devour them, if the difference means anything to Her - curtailing the explorations of the Begotten in her Land. However, there is a way to guard against the Mother's terrible love: to embrace the mythology of humanity and clothe yourself in it as armour, much like how the strange and powerful magi wrap themselves in their ego and self-image.<br /> <br /> This Merit grants the Beast an effective Amnion, which she can clothe herself in with an Instant action provided she has demonstrated her Legend this scene, granting general armor equal to her rating in Humanity's Monster against attacks that appear physical, and against the Ecstatic Wind. This pseudo-Amnion is treated as a form of equipment. It doesn\u2019t stack with \u201cphysical\u201d armor, but does stack with Atavisms such as Unbreakable and similar mystical powers. However, this does come with a drawback. As an embracing of her Horror's Legend and human side as opposed to its primal power, she suffers a -2 to rolls to activate Atavisms.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Beneath the Monster's Shadow (OOO)</b></u><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Humanity's Monster 3<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Monsters are creatures of terrible power - it is their nature - but so too are there monsters whose myths name them as protectors and guardians. A Beast can apply the same principles as imposing Lair Traits to protect their companions. Upon purchasing this Merit, the Beast gains the ability to forgo the normal effect of Mother's Kiss to instead grant the recipient the effects of Humanity's Monster for the scene. The Beast must have her pseudo-Amnion active in order to choose this alternative effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 05-24-2018, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T08:50:40-07:00","id":1221721,"title":"","content":"A very rough alternative:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Don the Dragon's Mantle (\u2022 or \u2022\u2022)</b></u><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Family Ties with a mage.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The Beast draws forth the shape of her Horror, replacing the normal Dream Form she assumes outside of her Lair. By spending a dot of Satiety, her Power, Finesse, Resistance, and Size are treated as her Horror's without any additional dots conferred by her Lair rating until she leaves the Astral or returns to her Lair.<br /> <br /> Taking this shape allows her to spend a point of Willpower to negate any amount of damage done to her Dream Health by the effects of the Mother's Land, but she does not add her Satiety to rolls to use Nightmares or the Mother's Kiss Kinship ability while in this form.<br /> <br /> At two dots, she gains general Armor against the effects of the Mother's Land equal to her Occult rating, and if she is &quot;killed&quot; by the Mother's Land, she may sacrifice a dot in this Merit rather than lose a Chamber from her Lair (Sanctity of Merits applies). Sacrificing a dot in this Merit in this way inflicts the Deprived Condition on the Beast, which resolves the next time she gains Satiety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-24-2018, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T08:45:10-07:00","id":1223273,"title":"","content":"So, Beast's can already configure their Chamber &quot;layout&quot; to restrict access to the Heart Chamber. Would there be niche for a Merit that sets up a &quot;locked door&quot; situation for the Heart Chamber, where they Key(s) are hidden in the other Chambers?<br /> <br /> The idea is that even if Intruders enter at a Chamber adjacent to the Heart, they can't just rush in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-30-2018, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T09:26:15-07:00","id":1223291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1223273#post1223273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Beast's can already configure their Chamber &quot;layout&quot; to restrict access to the Heart Chamber. Would there be niche for a Merit that sets up a &quot;locked door&quot; situation for the Heart Chamber, where they Key(s) are hidden in the other Chambers?<br /> <br /> The idea is that even if Intruders enter at a Chamber adjacent to the Heart, they can't just rush in.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a cool idea to me, although I'm not sure what dot-rating ti should be. Maybe dot-rating is related to the number of Keys you need to open the Heart?<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> And now I'm thinking of<i> Kingdom Hearts</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T11:59:31-07:00","id":1223347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1223291#post1223291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like a cool idea to me, although I'm not sure what dot-rating ti should be. Maybe dot-rating is related to the number of Keys you need to open the Heart?<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> And now I'm thinking of<i> Kingdom Hearts</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;What's this? A boy, a duck, and a... dog(?) have invaded my Lair? Should be easy pickings.&quot;<br /> [Short while later]<br /> &quot;Hey, Tony just dropped dead!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T17:38:48-07:00","id":1223442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1223273#post1223273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea is that even if Intruders enter at a Chamber adjacent to the Heart, they can't just rush in.</div> </div> </div> </div>The situation you are describing is the normal state of affairs for uninvited guests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T18:11:17-07:00","id":1223455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1223442#post1223442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The situation you are describing is the normal state of affairs for uninvited guests.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast: The Primordial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Intruders, on the other hand, must cope with any Tilts in effect and have to force their way through Burrows by spending a point of Willpower and succeeding on an Intelligence + Resolve roll contested by the Horror\u2019s Power + Resistance (see below). Forcing one\u2019s way through a Burrow takes half the Beast\u2019s Lair (round up) in turns, during which time the intruder is still subject to any Tilts in the Chamber he is trying to leave. Heroes, of course, have ways to mitigate these difficulties (see Chapter Five)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of those rules - they do not reflect what I am talking about. An intruder who manages to cross over at the Chamber that has a Burrow leading to the Heart Chamber only has to win that one Contested, <s>Extended</s> action to breach the Beast's defenses and try to take out the Heart. What I am talking about is they <i>cannot</i> make the attempt to reach the Heart Chamber unless they acquire [X] Key(s).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":".  Re-read and realized the action isn't actually Extended, it mere takes longer than a single turn. 07-31-2018, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T18:26:25-07:00","id":1223462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1223455#post1223455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware of those rules - they do not reflect what I am talking about. An intruder who manages to cross over at the Chamber that has a Burrow leading to the Heart Chamber only has to win that one Contested, Extended action to breach the Beast's defenses and try to take out the Heart. What I am talking about is they <i>cannot</i> make the attempt to reach the Heart Chamber unless they acquire [X] Key(s).</div> </div> </div> </div>And why exactly should a character actually bother with this when Willpower is a limited resource, sustained exposure to Lair Traits is often deadly, and all it takes for a Beast to double the amount of time it takes to get to the Heart is to redefine their Burrows back-to-front?<br /> <br /> Like, I get that this is a fun Dungeon Boss Monster idea, but what actual step of this process is not accomplished by the very simple and mundane process of having the Sealed Exits Trait and/or actual mundane locked thresholds within your Chambers that you've made supernaturally durable and put the keys to in a different place?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T11:13:00-07:00","id":1234051,"title":"","content":"Lifestealer (ooo)<br /> Prerequisite: Lair 3<br /> <br /> When attacking via Brawl, the character can take a -3 to his dicepool to heal themselves by 1 Bashing upon succesfully attacking.<br /> In addition, the player may chose to forego 10-again to upgrade the damage healed to 1 Lethal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I want some more help with that one - I am sure you can tell where I'm going with this. As an alternative to the homebrew Draining Kiss, Lifedrinker and Parasite Atavisms<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T16:08:03-07:00","id":1234106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1234051#post1234051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lifestealer (ooo)<br /> Prerequisite: Lair 3<br /> <br /> When attacking via Brawl, the character can take a -3 to his dicepool to heal themselves by 1 Bashing upon succesfully attacking.<br /> In addition, the player may chose to forego 10-again to upgrade the damage healed to 1 Lethal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I want some more help with that one - I am sure you can tell where I'm going with this. As an alternative to the homebrew Draining Kiss, Lifedrinker and Parasite Atavisms</div> </div> </div> </div>How about making it a kinship merit with vampires?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T13:06:09-07:00","id":1234372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1234106#post1234106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How about making it a kinship merit with vampires?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, that would work well!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T03:11:32-07:00","id":1240779,"title":"","content":"Random Thought: Lair Trait based Merits? Could those be a thing?<br /> <br /> E.g.<br /> <br /> Warming Up ooo<br /> Prerequisite: Extreme Heat Lair Trait<br /> <br /> Effect: Unlike other people and even Beasts, the Begotten is not merely able to stand heat, but outright thrives in it. When the Lair Trait applies, the Begotten becomes more nimble with time: what would have been a penalty instead acts as a bonus dicepool.<br /> Drawback: Cannot have Extreme Cold or Cold Performance<br /> <br /> <br /> Cold Performance ooo<br /> Prerequisite: Extreme Cold Lair Trait<br /> <br /> Effect: Unlike other people and even Beasts, the Begotten is not merely able to stand the cold, but runs at peak performance when it's freezing. When the Lair Trait applies, add the 8-again quality to rolls involving Intelligence.<br /> Drawback: Cannot have Extreme Hear or Warming Up<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T15:56:39-07:00","id":1241540,"title":"","content":"What would a merit that granted a Lair Trait to a single Chamber, couldn't be imposed on the outside world, and only grant you immunity in that specific Chamber cost? I'm thinking one or two because of how situational it is. I was thinking something like this could be nice as an option to further customize your Lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T18:05:43-07:00","id":1241603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1241540#post1241540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would a merit that granted a Lair Trait to a single Chamber, couldn't be imposed on the outside world, and only grant you immunity in that specific Chamber cost? I'm thinking one or two because of how situational it is. I was thinking something like this could be nice as an option to further customize your Lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually thinking that might be better as a kind of item you place in the chamber. Beast doesn't really have a magic-item/collectibles niche. That might be a useful thing for it - a kind of Lair Feng Shui/Interior Decorating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T05:24:06-07:00","id":1241769,"title":"","content":"Blood of the Beast ooo<br /> Bathing in the dragon's blood hardens the Heroes skin, blesses their blade, or can be used for occult purposes - this Begotten thought to himself: &quot;Why not just use it myself`?&quot;<br /> By taking 2 Lethal Damage and opening a wound to bleed from, they can harden an edge or make soft leather as durable as steel. Increase a weapon's rating by +3L, or add +2/1 to a piece of armor.<br /> They can also make use of their blood in Obcasus Rites and add +2 to the rolls, and their Mother's Kiss is more powerful as well: they add +3 to the roll.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T05:57:10-07:00","id":1241781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1241769#post1241769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood of the Beast ooo<br /> Bathing in the dragon's blood hardens the Heroes skin, blesses their blade, or can be used for occult purposes - this Begotten thought to himself: &amp;quot;Why not just use it myself`?&amp;quot;<br /> By taking 2 Lethal Damage and opening a wound to bleed from, they can harden an edge or make soft leather as durable as steel. Increase a weapon's rating by +3L, or add +2/1 to a piece of armor.<br /> They can also make use of their blood in Obcasus Rites and add +2 to the rolls, and their Mother's Kiss is more powerful as well: they add +3 to the roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why 2L? Usually this kind of sacrifice only needs 1L.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T09:02:43-07:00","id":1241857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1241781#post1241781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why 2L? Usually this kind of sacrifice only needs 1L.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Beast's have easy access to healing via Satiety Expenditure in their Lair, plus I think the Bonuses are quiet strong and most of all diverse enough to justify a slightly heavier-than-usual sacrifice<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T13:12:01-07:00","id":1242778,"title":"","content":"Hey one of my players is about to get a family bond with a Goblin Queen, any ideas for kinship merits with hobgoblins?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T17:06:54-07:00","id":1242822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1242778#post1242778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey one of my players is about to get a family bond with a Goblin Queen, any ideas for kinship merits with hobgoblins?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lots and lots of debt. Anything else is liable to need personalizing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T18:21:18-07:00","id":1242837,"title":"","content":"Merit concept: The Beast can copy goblin deals aka they can do minor magical services for people and in turn the client gets a form of goblin debt...but connected to the primordial dream as opposed to the hedge...Wut level would this be is what i wonder and is it feasible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T19:38:33-07:00","id":1242843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1242837#post1242837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Merit concept: The Beast can copy goblin deals aka they can do minor magical services for people and in turn the client gets a form of goblin debt...but connected to the primordial dream as opposed to the hedge...Wut level would this be is what i wonder and is it feasible?</div> </div> </div> </div>Suggested Name: <b>Dark Deals</b><br /> Mechanical effects: Target can accept the Leveraged or [Feeding Ground] (Target becomes priority one for a Horror's Dream Feeding) Condition, in exchange for a Mother's Kiss bonus to <i>any</i> roll, as loosely determined when the bargain is struck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T21:50:37-07:00","id":1242869,"title":"","content":"How about something like this:<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Fruit </b>(**)<br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Family ties with a Hob Goblin, Goblin King/Queen or a similar Hedge Denizen.<br /> <b>Description: </b>Since you began associating with your strange edge dwelling friend unusual plants have taken root in your Lair. They bear the tell-tale thorny profile of the Hedge and take root and thrive despite seemingly hostile conditions. Whatever dream from Arcadia they sprang from they are now adapting to your own nightmarescape. When you sate your hunger they grow fat on the powerful fear that courses through your Lair and produce bulbous fruits not dissimilar to those from the Hedge. But your friend is quick to point out, these are no Goblin Fruits. They swell with something more sinister. <br /> <b>Benefit: </b>When you successfully sate your Hunger and move from the Starving to Sated, or Sated to Gorged Condition you may choose not to take a single point of Satiety and instead &quot;store&quot; this in your Dread Fruit. The Dread Fruit may hold Satiety up to your Lair Rating. Once per Story any Beast (or with Storyteller discretion, similar creature) may consume the Dread Fruit inside your Lair to gain the Satiety stored within.<br /> <br /> Pretty rough first draft typed directly into the chat, could probably use some polish. Thoughts on balance/usefulness?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The ego is not king of its own castle.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13329-strictura","name":"Strictura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13329_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T22:21:50-07:00","id":1242874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strictura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1242869#post1242869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about something like this:<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Fruit </b>(**)<br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Family ties with a Hob Goblin, Goblin King/Queen or a similar Hedge Denizen.<br /> <b>Description: </b>Since you began associating with your strange edge dwelling friend unusual plants have taken root in your Lair. They bear the tell-tale thorny profile of the Hedge and take root and thrive despite seemingly hostile conditions. Whatever dream from Arcadia they sprang from they are now adapting to your own nightmarescape. When you sate your hunger they grow fat on the powerful fear that courses through your Lair and produce bulbous fruits not dissimilar to those from the Hedge. But your friend is quick to point out, these are no Goblin Fruits. They swell with something more sinister. <br /> <b>Benefit: </b>When you successfully sate your Hunger and move from the Starving to Sated, or Sated to Gorged Condition you may choose not to take a single point of Satiety and instead &quot;store&quot; this in your Dread Fruit. The Dread Fruit may hold Satiety up to your Lair Rating. Once per Story any Beast (or with Storyteller discretion, similar creature) may consume the Dread Fruit inside your Lair to gain the Satiety stored within.<br /> <br /> Pretty rough first draft typed directly into the chat, could probably use some polish. Thoughts on balance/usefulness?</div> </div> </div> </div>You should also add Hunger Management as a prerequisite, to indicate the Beast's inclination to plan out their meals.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, it sounds like a really awesome merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;To succeed, planning alone is insufficient. One must improvise as well.&quot; - Salvor Hardin, Foundation</span></span></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13444-zannmato","name":"zannmato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T22:23:37-07:00","id":1242875,"title":"","content":"Good idea, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The ego is not king of its own castle.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13329-strictura","name":"Strictura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13329_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T10:45:42-07:00","id":1252277,"title":"","content":"<b>Imitation of Life (\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Family Ties with a Fetch or Promethean<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The character is shielded from supernatural powers that would detect her as anything but human. Dice rolls for such powers enter a Clash of Wills against a dicepool of character\u2019s Lair + highest Resistance Attribute. This Merit also affects uses of Family Resemblance, making the character count as \u201cfundamentally human\u201d and possibly subtracting his Satiety from investigator\u2019s dice pool (B:tP p.88).<br /> <br /> <b>Empty Words (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Family Ties with an Acartharos<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Words spoken by the character have no metaphysical weight whatsoever. This offers him a measure of protection against certain supernatural effects. She can\u2019t be bound by an oath based upon her declarations, curses triggered by uttering a secret do not activate and truth-detecting effects outright ignore her confessions.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> There is a specific circumstance under which this effect is suspended. Use Bans and Banes as inspiration. The character can exploit this exception for his own benefit, but it can be used against him should the secret ever come out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T11:08:49-07:00","id":1252286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1252277#post1252277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Empty Words (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Family Ties with an Acartharos<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Words spoken by the character have no metaphysical weight whatsoever. This offers him a measure of protection against certain supernatural effects. She can\u2019t be bound by an oath based upon her declarations, curses triggered by uttering a secret do not activate and truth-detecting effects outright ignore her confessions.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> There is a specific circumstance under which this effect is suspended. Use Bans and Banes as inspiration. The character can exploit this exception for his own benefit, but it can be used against him should the secret ever come out.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's an Acartharos? Do you mean Acanthus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 09-07-2018, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T11:15:26-07:00","id":1252289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What's an Acartharos? Do you mean Acanthus? </div> </div> </div>Akathartoi were introduced in Mage 1E (Imperial Mysteries, i think). They're creatures populating the Lower Depths, assimilable to the &quot;True&quot; Demons from the Inferno Sourcebook (beings thriving off sin and possessing people, not fugitives fleeing the God-Machine).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T11:20:14-07:00","id":1252291,"title":"","content":"Correct! The Merit is supposed to be a knock-off of their position as perfect liars. I would have used the Unchained except... you know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T19:58:59-07:00","id":1252425,"title":"","content":"<b>Multi-Headed (* or ***):</b> Your horror possesses conjoined siblings that take the form of additional heads. Each head possesses its own level of sentience and shows a willingness to collaborate with each other... most of the time, anyways.<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> At least 1 alternate personality.<br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> At the 1 dot level of this merit, the Beast is fully aware of the existence of any split personalities they possess, and they may share information between each other, even while the others lay dormant. At the 3 dot level of this merit, the Beast may freely transition between which personality is in control of their body. Which can prove invaluable if one of the other personalities has a particular set of skills that the current one is lacking in.<br /> <br /> If the Beast obtains any additional personalities later on in life, their horror manifests an additional head to represent the new consciousness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-09-2018, 07:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T09:31:11-07:00","id":1252526,"title":"","content":"How would you design a merit that allowed a Beast to gain a Wolf-Blooded Tell? Begotten can already have them if they were Wolf-Blooded before the Devouring, but a way to pick them up after the fact would be cool.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm overthinking it, and you should just be able to buy the Tell merit as if it were a Werewolf Kinship merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T13:09:35-07:00","id":1252583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1252526#post1252526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm overthinking it, and you should just be able to buy the Tell merit as if it were a Werewolf Kinship merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>That one, I think. Why add more than necessary?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T22:52:19-07:00","id":1252674,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Twin-Souled (Creation Only) OOOO or OOOOO</b></u><br /> <br /> Rather than one, your Beast has two Horrors, of the same or with 5 O even of different Families!<br /> This allows them easier access to Atavisms (if both of the same Family -&gt; In-Family Atavisms cost 1 xp less, if different Families --&gt; twice as many In-Family purchases) and makes defending their Lair much easier (both Horrors act as seperate characters), which is bound to surprise any Hero expecting one Horror only. It also grants the Twin-Souled an additional two Atavisms, as each Horror has their own seperate Atavisms.<br /> With 5 dots, Feeding is also easier, since the Beast can express their Hunger through different Families.<br /> Finally, they can more easily resist Anathema if the Hero in question didn't do enough research, gaining a +2 to relevant traits (e.g. Defense) where applicable.<br /> However, this comes at a price: The Lair is not big enough to fully sustain two Horrors to their full potential, so when calculating the Horror's stats, they need to share the 2*Lair bonus points, each getting half. Furthermore, when Feeding, 1 Satiety gets lost to the Horror's squabbling over the meal, and two Horrors burn through the Satiety twice as fast: A Lair 1-3 Beast loses one Satiety every three days, 4-6 every other day, 7-9 every day, and Lair 10 Twin-Souled would lose 2 Satiety per day. Atavisms are bought per Horror, so buying Unbreakable only applies to one Horror, which can influence fights within the Lair heavily. Atavisms do not stack. If both Horrors are of the same Family, learning out-of-Family Atavisms becomes harder: pay an additional 1 xp. Finally, unlike other Beasts, the Twin-Souled may be subject to two Anathema at any given time.<br /> <br /> <br /> Essentially, this is an early power boost with immense drawbacks. Might be a fun merit for a chronicle or two, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T18:37:22-07:00","id":1252895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1252674#post1252674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Twin-Souled (Creation Only) OOOO or OOOOO</b></u></div> </div> </div> </div>That is a lot of stuff (both pros and cons) packed into a single Merit.<br /> <br /> I would do a Standard/Advanced/Epic version, personally, or a minor template modification and accompanying Merit set, like the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1e43wIzNAHTlmyhnwNcE58ZzPQpPKzBOdF1C3eZVRbsU/edit#heading=h.seo0depfknny\" target=\"_blank\">Soulbound</a> I made for mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-28T12:50:37-07:00","id":1257819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1252895#post1252895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is a lot of stuff (both pros and cons) packed into a single Merit.<br /> <br /> I would do a Standard/Advanced/Epic version, personally, or a minor template modification and accompanying Merit set, like the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1e43wIzNAHTlmyhnwNcE58ZzPQpPKzBOdF1C3eZVRbsU/edit#heading=h.seo0depfknny\" target=\"_blank\">Soulbound</a> I made for mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good food for thought, will revise.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Myth over Physics OOOO</u></b><br /> <i>Prerequisite: Cyclopean Strength AND Crushing Coils</i><br /> <br /> Being strong enough to lift an airplane is a great ability - however, as many Beast's had come to realize, Superman physics don't apply to the real world, and from a certain size onward, their improvised weaponry tended to break apart. As usefull as it would be as a clubbering weapons, cars had a tendency to come off at the bumper or tire when swung around, and statues gave in to their own weight, leaving the Begotten usually with just a small boulder.<br /> That is, unless they draw upon their Horror to stabilize their enourmous weapon - even when wielding something like the Empire State Building, held together by the World Serpent Jormungandr, it stays intact as a weapon.<br /> Mechanically, the Begotten has to spent a point of Willpower, which allows them to lift something to the upper limits of their ability as a non-crumbling weapon. The most obvious benefit here is that with some luck, a Begotten can attack a number of enemies at the same time, like autofire. There are benefits to wielding an airplane as a club other than reach, however: the weapon gains a modifier of + (1/5 its size). When going over +5, the weapon instead starts at +1 Aggravated. Since these weapons are very cumbersome to use, the Begotten reduces their Initiative by (1/3 size). If this would reduce their Initiative below 0, they start gaining a penalty to the attack roll (to a maximum of -5). Depending on the scene, friendly characters have to dodge if an attack in their vicinity takes place, because the weapon does not differentiate friend from foe.<br /> The enhancement works for a scene, but applies only to the one weapon - dropping it to use something else (e.g. because it was destroyed) means another WP expenditure is necessary.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Example:<br /> During the Battle for Ellis Island between two Broods, the Statue of Liberty was detached at its base and falling over. The legendary Anakim Apex Jorel managed to get hold of the statue at the top of the torch, and proceeded to use it as a grotesquely oversized club against the enemy. Against all common sense, it did not break of at the arm, because Jorel drew on his Horror to hold it together.<br /> Jorel's player wants to take out the enemy Brood's Werewolf, because he's tanking a lot but also is already wounded heavily. Due to the size of his 'club', he acts last, but thank's to his Makara Broodmate's helpful use of Monster from the Deep, most of the other group was unable to move this turn. Due to the drawbacks Jorel rolls an abysmall dicepool of 2, but lucks out and gets a success - with the weapon's modifier and the accumulated damage so far, he manages to deal a killing blow.<br /> Even an Uratha's regenerative ability in War Form was no match to a lucky blow with the monument. The rest managed to move out of the way just fine, however, and decided to retreat for the day and plot their revenge.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Needs work, I know, it's a first draft, but I think you get the general idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-15T04:43:42-07:00","id":1260645,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Know no Fear oo or ooo</b></u><br /> <br /> Either through instinct, training or experience, this Hero knows how to fight Beasts while avoiding to fall prey to their Nightmare abilities. By taking a -2 to fighting actions, they manage to reflexively avoid eye contact, while being still able to predict attacks and strike on their own. Beasts who are not aware of this, e.g. because the Hero wears sunglasses inside like a douche, will simply waste their time and energy while the Hero has the suprise advantage. With three dots, there is no penalty to fighting actions.<br /> There are rumours of a scattering of Hunters learning this, too, though the skill is much rarer among them.<br /> <br /> Drawback: This instinct cannot be turned off - their behaviour comes off as strange to others, which is why they often develop a cover story for why they do not hold eye contact. All social actions are penalized by -2 (-1 with a good enough cover story).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T05:35:42-08:00","id":1289874,"title":"","content":"Not a merit, but a condition concept I'm playing around with and didn't know where else to post:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Ghouled</b></u><br /> Kindred Vitae is powerful and has many applications, but other than making them addicted, it usually has no effect on Begotten. Humans, however, can benefit vastly, to the point of acquiring vampiric Disciplines.<br /> It is possible for Begotten to enjoy these benefits (with the accompanying drawbacks), too. Properly preperated, Kindred Vitae can be used to give or force upon a Begotten access to the mortal state of Ghouldom.<br /> This requires a stronger physical presence, however, leaving their link to their ephemeral Horror disjointed.<br /> Mechanically, the Beast loses their Atavisms and gains the minor-Template of a Ghoul. The Horror loses Satiety as if it were one tier higher (Someone with Lair 1-3 would lose Satiety at the rate of someone at Lair 4-6) and Feeding starts with a modifier of -1. The ghouled Begotten may pay Vitae instead of Satiety to fuel their Nightmares. The Horror acts as a seperate Ephemeral Entity for the time, and tries to provide for itself.<br /> <br /> This will invariably lead to Inversion or Divergence, as the Horror will grow increasingly antagonistic, so the Begotten may have additional incentive to end this state (or follow through, if they so wish). Choosing Vitae over Satiety leads to a Lair roll. Upon success, they lose a Satiety.<br /> <br /> <br /> Beats: When the Horror causes lasting trouble to the Begotten (e.g. by attacking their close ones)<br /> Condition ends when the Vitae-providing vampire is destroyed, or one month after the last dose of Vitae, or when the Begotten confronts their Horror (followed up by Inheritance).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T13:07:38-08:00","id":1290504,"title":"","content":"Minor problem with that-nothing says that a Beast <i>can't</i> be ghouled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T14:55:19-08:00","id":1290544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1290504#post1290504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minor problem with that-nothing says that a Beast <i>can't</i> be ghouled.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Makes the merit seem even better to me. The only mention of the process requiring unusual circumstances is in the fluff. The mechanics seem great to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T14:57:02-08:00","id":1290546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1290504#post1290504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minor problem with that-nothing says that a Beast <i>can't</i> be ghouled.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always felt splat stacking was in bad taste myself, so this merit works for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T15:00:01-08:00","id":1290547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1290546#post1290546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've always felt splat stacking was in bad taste myself, so this merit works for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still splat mixing. I'm pretty sure it even implies they can get disciplines like a ghoul. Just adding unique features and mixing and matching powers instead of just Making a Beast + Ghoul. Now it's a .... huh, I can't really think of any mathematical functions that work to metaphorically explain how this is different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T16:19:40-08:00","id":1290581,"title":"","content":"Splat stacking being in bad taste is a matter of person. But just as nothing stops you from being a wolf-blooded mage or a demon-blooded Sin-Eater, nothing stops you from being a ghouled Beast.<br /> <br /> (there are some stacking that beg a question in terms of canon interactions, but too much more dives into a different conversation)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T05:34:29-08:00","id":1290724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1290547#post1290547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's still splat mixing. I'm pretty sure it even implies they can get disciplines like a ghoul. Just adding unique features and mixing and matching powers instead of just Making a Beast + Ghoul. Now it's a .... huh, I can't really think of any mathematical functions that work to metaphorically explain how this is different.</div> </div> </div> </div>It provides a cost and a benefit, both mechanically, and in roleplay. This gives some semblance of balance.<br /> <br /> And I'm quite aware it's personal preference. That's why I noted it worked for me. To get the benefits of a minor template, I like there to be a cost. This merit provides an acceptable cost for a benefit. And you won't see stacking major splats at all in my games.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I love to mix it up, but mixing splats is kinda like playing gestalt- some people like it, others don't. I'm just in the latter category.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T03:23:24-08:00","id":1292425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1290504#post1290504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minor problem with that-nothing says that a Beast <i>can't</i> be ghouled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I think that was a homerule. Should've mentioned that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T09:48:44-08:00","id":1292515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1292425#post1292425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, I think that was a homerule. Should've mentioned that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a home rule that Beasts can't be ghouled?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T09:53:44-08:00","id":1292521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1292515#post1292515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a home rule that Beasts can't be ghouled?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe the term was house rule?<br /> They cannot be Ghouled as such - they get addicted and the intense attraction/emotional bond, but not the 'supernatural benefits' like access to Disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T11:02:44-08:00","id":1292535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1292521#post1292521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Maybe the term was house rule?<br /> They cannot be Ghouled as such - they get addicted and the intense attraction/emotional bond, but not the 'supernatural benefits' like access to Disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either one is fine.<br /> <br /> It just.<br /> <br /> I don't get this decision in the context of the conversation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T20:26:21-07:00","id":1315365,"title":"","content":"For those of you who dislike the fact that only Incarnates can turn others into stone.<br /> <br /> Namtaru Birthright: Once per scene, the Beast may spend 1 Satiety as an Instant Action to petrify all characters who gaze upon him. Roll Presence + Intimidation or Occult. This lasts for a number of turns equal to Successes + Lair. The victims remain petrified for the rest of the scene and have an effective Durability of 5. They also remain fully conscious, aware of their surroundings and may be moved. Potential victims instinctively know that they can avoid being petrified by closing their eyes. During this, they suffer the Blinded Tilt on both eyes and the Beast may take advantage of that fact. While inside the Lair or otherwise fused with the Horror, there is no need to spend Satiety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-05-2020, 06:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T11:14:29-07:00","id":1316665,"title":"","content":"<b>Sorcerer's Insight (\u2022 To \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Mimir's Wisdom, Needs Must, Family Ties With A Mage, Wits <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022, </b>Occult \u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Effect:</b> When the Beast needs to roll for a Clash Of Wills using Needs Must, he gains bonus dice equal to the rating in this Merit. If the Clash Of Wills is successful, he may spend 1 Willpower point as a reflexive action to ask a number of yes or no questions about the target equal to rating in this Merit. The ST must answer truthfully. If the Clash Of Wills received an Exceptional Success, the Beast does not need to spend Willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Advanced Sorcerer's Insight (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Sorcerer's Insight, Wits <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, </b>Occult \u2022\u2022<b>\u2022</b><br /> <b>Effect: </b>The basic version of the Merit now achieves Exceptional Success with 3 Successes.<br /> <br /> <b>Slip Through The Shackles Of Fate (\u2022 To \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Family Ties With An Acanthus, Mummy Or Changeling, Wits <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022, </b>Occult \u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Effect: </b>Any supernatural attempt at foreseeing or altering the Beast's future, as well as force him into any sort of contract, bargain or oath, trigger a Clash Of Wills with bonus dice equal to rating in this Merit. The Beast always knows when this Merit is being activated and has a general idea of the source's direction and distance. If the Clash Of Wills received an Exceptional Success, he also knows the precise location and exactly what the originator of the supernatural ability wanted to do to him. This may add +2 to Satiety Potential if the Beast uses this knowledge to Feed on the originator, but the Beast must do it within the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Advanced Slip Through The Shackles Of Fate (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Slip Through The Shackles Of Fate, Wits <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, </b>Occult \u2022\u2022<b>\u2022<br /> Effect: </b>The basic version of the Merit now achieves Exceptional Success with 3 Successes.<br /> <br /> <b>Skin-Changer (\u2022 To \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Family Ties With Any Supernatural Who Can Transform Into Animals, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1314995#post1314995\"><b>Lord Of Animals</b></a>, Stamina <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022, </b>Animal Ken \u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Effect: </b>The Beast can use Lord Of Animals to become his favored creatures himself. Any supernatural attempt at revealing or reverting him to his baseline self triggers a Clash Of Wills, with bonus dice equal to rating in this Merit. The Beast may skin a favored creature to bestow this Merit upon another, who use their own dice pool for the Clash Of Wills but still gain bonus dice equal to the rating of the Merit. If the target has no dice pool for a Clash Of Wills, he rolls Stamina + Animal Ken + rating in this Merit.<br /> <br /> Each such skin can only be used once and lasts for the scene, but the character may revert to his baseline self earlier by spending 1 Willpower point as an Instant Action. The transformation is frequently a Breaking Point for mortals. Regardless of the creature that the character becomes, he uses his own Size to for the purposes of calculating Health and suffering Tilts like Stunned. However, while wearing the skin, the character gains the benefits on relevant rolls for the form he is assuming, as listed under Lord Of Animals. The Beast may even &quot;skin&quot; creatures such as arthropods by finding a bunch of them and preparing an ointment with their innards.<br /> <br /> <b>Advanced Skin-Changer (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite: </b>Skin-Changer, Stamina <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, </b>Animal Ken \u2022\u2022<b>\u2022<br /> Effect: </b>The skin fuses with the character's form once worn, but outwardly he looks the same. He may freely shift between the creature and baseline forms as a reflexive action. The Beast must spend 1 Satiety when preparing the skin, and it fuses with the target for a number of days equal to the Beast's Lair x 2.<br /> <br /> <b>Eshmaki Birthright:</b> Once per scene, the Beast can reflexively vanish and reappear within the immediate vicinity of the nearest individual who is suffering from a Condition that represents fear, such as Spooked, Shaken or Frightened. The Beast gains Rote Quality to ambush the victim. However, the Beast does not know where he will manifest in advance, and characters with supernatural means of detecting ambushes may trigger a Clash Of Wills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-05-2020, 06:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T12:43:16-08:00","id":1349148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1223273#post1223273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Beast's can already configure their Chamber &amp;quot;layout&amp;quot; to restrict access to the Heart Chamber. Would there be niche for a Merit that sets up a &amp;quot;locked door&amp;quot; situation for the Heart Chamber, where they Key(s) are hidden in the other Chambers?<br /> <br /> The idea is that even if Intruders enter at a Chamber adjacent to the Heart, they can't just rush in.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1223291#post1223291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like a cool idea to me, although I'm not sure what dot-rating ti should be. Maybe dot-rating is related to the number of Keys you need to open the Heart?<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> And now I'm thinking of<i> Kingdom Hearts</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here\u2019s my attempt at making the above a reality. Everyone who\u2019s reading this <b><u><i>AND</i></u></b> has an account is free to change, alter, refine, improve, etc upon it.<br /> <br /> <b>Locked Heart (\u2022-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Beast, Lair 8+<br /> <b>Effect</b>: The path into the Beast\u2019s Heart Chamber is blocked by a Lock of some kind, as detailed by the Player upon acquiring the Merit. Attempts to pick the Lock suffer a malus of -1, cumulatively increasing per dot rating to a maximum of -5, though the malus <i>can</i> be lessened by having one or more of the Keys. The number of Keys needed to open the Lock is equal to the dot rating, but the Keys themselves are hidden throughout the Lair.<br /> <br /> Example; Zack Nortek, a lone Hunter, is trying to reach the Heart Chamber of Arthur Malporgan, a local Beast. Fortunately for Arthur, his Player recently managed to acquire the Locked Heart Merit at 3 dots. Zack\u2019s Player, upon realising this, immediately has Zack start rummaging around for the requisite Keys. Unfortunately, he rolls poorly enough for Zack to only find one of them, so he defaults to trying to pick the Lock. With the Merit at a rating of 3, the attempt gets an automatic -3 deduction. Thankfully, he has a Key, so the Malus is lessened to -2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T15:40:31-08:00","id":1349180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1349148#post1349148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Here\u2019s my attempt at making the above a reality. Everyone who\u2019s reading this <b><u><i>AND</i></u></b> has an account is free to change, alter, refine, improve, etc upon it.<br /> <br /> <b>Locked Heart (\u2022-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Beast, Lair 8+<br /> <b>Effect</b>: The path into the Beast\u2019s Heart Chamber is blocked by a Lock of some kind, as detailed by the Player upon acquiring the Merit. Attempts to pick the Lock suffer a malus of -1, cumulatively increasing per dot rating to a maximum of -5, though the malus <i>can</i> be lessened by having one or more of the Keys. The number of Keys needed to open the Lock is equal to the dot rating, but the Keys themselves are hidden throughout the Lair.<br /> <br /> Example; Zack Nortek, a lone Hunter, is trying to reach the Heart Chamber of Arthur Malporgan, a local Beast. Fortunately for Arthur, his Player recently managed to acquire the Locked Heart Merit at 3 dots. Zack\u2019s Player, upon realising this, immediately has Zack start rummaging around for the requisite Keys. Unfortunately, he rolls poorly enough for Zack to only find one of them, so he defaults to trying to pick the Lock. With the Merit at a rating of 3, the attempt gets an automatic -3 deduction. Thankfully, he has a Key, so the Malus is lessened to -2.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd lower the Lair rating of the thing, and I'd probably also make it explicit that Locks can take a lot of different forms - a river that's nigh-impossible to ford, a wall of ravening flame, a simple <b>actual </b>wall etc..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T15:45:21-08:00","id":1349184,"title":"","content":"I understand it from context, but is malus a term from the Beast Player's Guide? Otherwise, it seems like unnecessary jargon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T06:04:21-08:00","id":1349560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1349180#post1349180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd lower the Lair rating of the thing, and I'd probably also make it explicit that Locks can take a lot of different forms - a river that's nigh-impossible to ford, a wall of ravening flame, a simple <b>actual </b>wall etc..</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll take your (thankfully constructive) criticisms into account and further refine the Merit. Thank you for the help.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1349184#post1349184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand it from context, but is malus a term from the Beast Player's Guide? Otherwise, it seems like unnecessary jargon.</div> </div> </div> </div>The term isn't from the Beast Player's Guide, but a term I've heard used in other RPGs, as well as various Video Games. I used it because I can't remember the Chronicles of Darkness's equivalent term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T06:06:36-08:00","id":1349561,"title":"","content":"Penalty works. Sorry for being too brusque. I was in a rush","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T07:32:17-08:00","id":1350642,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Now I want to up the Legend of Zelda references even more and add some way for characters to get &quot;treasures&quot; from Chambers. But that would be almost an entire sub-system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T12:40:40-08:00","id":1353927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1349561#post1349561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Penalty works. Sorry for being too brusque. I was in a rush</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I\u2019ll be sure to make the necessary corrections in the refined version of the merit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1350642#post1350642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Now I want to up the Legend of Zelda references even more and add some way for characters to get &amp;quot;treasures&amp;quot; from Chambers. But that would be almost an entire sub-system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Maybe you could make a thread for that? I give you full permission to take as much inspiration from the Locked Heart merit as you feel is necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T05:31:26-08:00","id":1372135,"title":"","content":"<u><i><b>Primordial Blacksmith Style</b></i></u><br /> Prerequisites: Beast, Mimir's Wisdom, Burning Lair Trait, Obcasus Initiate, Lair Equal To Style Rating<br /> <br /> (\u2022): The Beast can perform Crafting Equipment rolls that fall within the Blacksmith Specialty using his bare hands. He still needs suitable raw materials, but adds (Style Rating) to the roll. His touch serves as a source of heat, torque and so on. The Beast can only use this Style outside of locations that he has prepared via the Consecrate Rite by making a blood offering of 1 Resistant Lethal. These Crafting Equipment rolls stack with the Rote Quality given by the Low Satiety of Mimir's Wisdom.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022): By spending 1 Willpower, the Beast can turn the relevant Crafting Equipment roll into an Instant Action. This does not add +3 dice and can only be done once per scene.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022): The Beast considers the presence of the Burning Lair Trait as being suitable raw materials. He essentially feeds inert matter into the flames, which is broken down and transmuted into usable ores.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): When spending Satiety for Mimir's Wisdom, the Beast may generate 1 dot of Advanced Library. The resulting Informed Condition must be related to the Blacksmith Specialty and also the Hunger in some way. For example: a Tyrant could use it to craft a terrifying sword for dueling other monsters, while a Collector can craft wondrous jewelry for luring and bribing victims. <br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): The Beast can infuse the items he creates with the essence of the Primordial Dream. The result is a Relic, which imposes a penalty to the Crafting Equipment roll equal to (Relic's Rating). The Beast must have Family Ties with a monster who displays supernatural abilities similar to those he wishes to place inside the Relic, or display such abilities himself. This lasts for the scene. If the Beast gets an Exceptional Success, he can make the Relic permanent by spending Satiety equal to its Rating. The maximum number of permanent Relics that can be created by spending Satiety is (Style Rating) + Resolve. Each additional permanent Relic requires the sacrifice of a Willpower Dot.<br /> <br /> Note: Other versions of this Style exist, which are linked to different Lair Traits and Skill Specialties. For example, you could have a Namtaru which makes cursed potions via this Style. The Lair Trait could be Toxic and the Skill Specialty would be Toxicology in Medicine. Consider using <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar775_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"775\" data-vbnamecard=\"775\">Reighnhell</a>'s <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes?p=1331652#post1331652\">Guidelines For Relics.</a> </b>If you think the Fifth Maneuver might be excessive, feel free to limit it to once per Chapter. Every Relic created via this Style must include at least one Drawback related to the Beast's Hunger, usually a Condition or Tilt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-13-2020, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T12:44:54-07:00","id":1373802,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\">GibberingEloquence</a> very nice!</b></span></span><br /> </span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T14:52:02-07:00","id":1375148,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Drain The Well (\u2022 Or \u2022\u2022)</b></u><br /> <i>Prerequisites: Beast, Find A Vein 3 (Any), Occult 2, Obcasus Initiate<br /> <br /> The Beast can draw upon the mystical lifeblood of his Kin to aid in his nightmarish sorcery. By spending 5 units of metaphysical energy from the Vein, you receive 8 Again on the next roll of the Extended Action. With the 2 dot version of this Merit, this expenditure gives Rote Quality on the next roll instead. <br /> <br /> Drawback: The Beast must drink voraciously from the Primordial Dream, which runs the risk of his Horror developing a taste for the fear of his Kin. Upon completion of the Obcasus Rite, the Beast must roll Resolve + Composure - (Find A Vein Rating). On a Failure, the Beast can only regain Satiety if he feeds upon a monster associated with the metaphysical energy contained in his Vein, with a Satiety Potential of at least [Lair]. After gaining Satiety this way, your Hunger may be sated by Feeding on other targets normally.<br /> <br /> Note: Check the original post of this thread for the Find A Vein Merit.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-05-2020, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T17:48:16-07:00","id":1375189,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> Any thoughts on the Merit I posted right above? I'm curious about how you would do it, since you're the one who wrote Find A Vein.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T03:24:20-07:00","id":1375243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1375189#post1375189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> Any thoughts on the Merit I posted right above? I'm curious about how you would do it, since you're the one who wrote Find A Vein.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I can weigh in, I might suggest putting a time-limit on the whole 'getting a taste for Kin' thing, rather than making it permanent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T03:36:05-07:00","id":1375244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1375243#post1375243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I can weigh in, I might suggest putting a time-limit on the whole 'getting a taste for Kin' thing, rather than making it permanent.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh it is not meant to be permanent. Once you Feed your Hunger on your Kin as described in the Merit, your Hunger returns to normal. I'll edit it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T03:43:00-07:00","id":1375247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1375244#post1375244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh it is not meant to be permanent. Once you Feed your Hunger on your Kin as described in the Merit, your Hunger returns to normal. I'll edit it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes a lot more sense. It did seem a little punishing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T06:13:58-07:00","id":1375271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1375148#post1375148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By spending units of metaphysical energy from the Vein equal to <b>[Level of the Obcasus Rite x 5]</b>, you achieve 1 automatic Success on the next roll of the Extended Action, plus the result on the roll, effectively lowering your threshold for Exceptional Success to 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that way too expensive? A two dot Rite would require a Lair rating of 6+ in order to be able to raise your Attributes, Occult and Merit ratings high enough to have enough of the fuel without having to refuel while performing the ritual. A three dot Rite would require a Lair rating of 10. Four and five dot Rites are impossible to boost without refuelling so you can spend more then your pool would allow. That's a lot of fuel on top of the Merit's significant drawback for a single automatic success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T06:43:15-07:00","id":1375276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1375271#post1375271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that way too expensive? A two dot Rite would require a Lair rating of 6+ in order to be able to raise your Attributes, Occult and Merit ratings high enough to have enough of the fuel without having to refuel while performing the ritual. A three dot Rite would require a Lair rating of 10. Four and five dot Rites are impossible to boost without refuelling so you can spend more then your pool would allow. That's a lot of fuel on top of the Merit's significant drawback for a single automatic success.</div> </div> </div> </div> By level I meant [Basic / Intermediate / Advanced / Epic], which would require [5 / 10 / 15 / 20] Vein points, respectively. But yeah, I get you. I'll lower it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T07:17:24-07:00","id":1375280,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I messed up in that they aren't dot rated (probably got it mixed up with Rites from WtF and Ceremonies from GtSE that both are dot rated). Still, most characters can only have a maximum fuel pool of 9. By using Epic Potential you can get your Presence/Stamina up to 6, and thus the Find a Vein Merit is limited to 4 dots, with an additional +5 from Occult dots.<br /> 6 Attribute dots, 5 Merit dots and 5 Skill dots is quite an investment. Plus technically another 2 Merit dots for Obcasus Initiate.<br /> <br /> I would recommend reducing the cost to equal the penalty that most Rites have on each level (3/4/6/8), or something like 3 plus one additional point per level above Basic Rites (3/4/5/6), or even using a flat cost of 4 or 5 points regardless of level. The cost should compare to the benefit, and the benefit of a single automatic success already decreases for each level because its impact gets smaller when the target number increases. Having a scaling cost only means you're not going to use it for the higher Rites, when it's those you have the most trouble succeeding with and should want to use this kind of advantage with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T01:44:14-07:00","id":1378698,"title":"","content":"<i><u><b>Colossal Horror (\u2022\u2022 Or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></u><br /> Prerequisite: Beast<br /> While inside the Lair or otherwise fused with the Horror, every dot of Horror Form you invest into Size gives +10 Size, up to five dots of investment. With the 4 dot version of this Merit, each dot invested into Horror Form gives +20 Size. Since your Corpus is equal to [Resistance Attribute + Trait Maximum Based On Lair], this humongous Size does not give extra Corpus.<br /> <br /> Instead, it simply allows you to make Brawl or Weaponry attacks from a distance of up to [Size] meters due to the absolutely massive reach of your horrific limbs. However, moving your monstrous bulk to hit from such a distance with enough speed requires considerable effort. This is represented as the Beast making an All-Out Attack.<br /> <br /> As a drawback, whenever a smaller opponent successfully Dodges this attack, you effectively suffer the Stunned Tilt. Any other effects must be bestowed by Atavisms or equivalent traits. At ST's discretion, other destructive Atavisms such as Titanic Blow and Dragonfire may also have their reach increased proportionally to your extra Size.<br /> <br /> In the edge case that an Atavism or similar ability requires the Beast to sacrifice Defense (e.g. Monster From The Deep), he does not need to choose between applying Colossal Horror or said Atavism; he benefits from both.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Diminutive Horror (\u2022\u2022 Or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></u><br /> Prerequisite: Beast<br /> While inside the Lair or otherwise fused with the Horror, you are a fixed Size 1 and cannot invest dots of Horror Form into Size. Instead, you scurry and lurk around like a twitchy insect or mischievous imp. You may invest dots of Horror Form directly into Speed. Each dot thus invested increases it by +10, up to five dots of investment. With the 4 dot version of this Merit, each dot invested into Horror Form gives +20 Speed. Since your Corpus is equal to [Resistance Attribute + Trait Maximum Based On Lair], this minimal Size does not decrease your Corpus. Furthermore, you can move your full Speed reflexively once per turn and also make an Instant Action, such as Dexterity + Stealth. You can squeeze through most nooks and crannies, and you do not have to move in a straight line: you can zigzag, climb up walls and so forth.<br /> <br /> As a drawback, whenever you move your full Speed in one turn, you produce creepy and unsettling noises themed after your Horror which can alert others to your presence. They receive 8 Again for Perception rolls made against you in such cases. If they already have another instance of 8 Again (such as through Trained Observer 3), they benefit from Rote Quality instead. </i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-12-2020, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T21:59:14-07:00","id":1380581,"title":"","content":"<u><i><b>Your Mother's Claws (Style, \u2022 To \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></i></u><br /> Prerequisites: Beast, Wits 3, Occult 2, Lair 2+<br /> <br /> (\u2022): Whenever you succeed on a roll for Family Resemblance, you may ask a number of yes/no questions about the target equal to [Style Rating]. You also add [Style Rating] on Clashes Of Wills involving Family Resemblance. These questions must be related to the target's Family or equivalent trait in some way. On an Exceptional Success, the Beast may also ask questions about the target's Hunger or equivalent trait. This Maneuver can help a savvy Beast prepare an opportunity for a Family Dinner.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022): By spending 1 Willpower upon using the previous Maneuver, each answer receives one sentence of additional context. This does not add +3 to the roll and may only be done once per scene.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022): The Beast achieves Exceptional Success with 3 Successes when rolling for Family Resemblance. If he has Family Ties with at least one monster of the same overall type as the one he is observing, add [Occult] to the number of questions the Beast can ask.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): The Beast gains an indefinite bonus of [Style Rating/2 Rounded Up] to Satiety Potential for any Feeding where the target is a supporting actor. The Beast has a maximum number of other monsters who give him this bonus equal to [Style Rating + Occult]. This list can be redefined at the start of each Chapter. Furthermore, whenever the Beast participates in a Family Dinner involving such monsters, he gains a positive Condition on top of the Satiety, such as Steadfast or Inspired.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): The Beast may now use Family Resemblance to scent out monsters in addition to identifying those she is already observing. This stacks with previous Maneuvers. Rolling normally, she may become aware of the shortest path towards a creature fitting up to (Successes) criteria on the same plane of existence, chosen from the list below. If she fails, she still becomes aware of a nearby monster, but has no particular information as to its nature. If she dramatically fails, instead a nearby monster becomes aware of her curiosity and locale.<br /> <br /> - Kinship: The Beast may select a kind of supernatural entity she is aware of, such as &quot;vampire,&quot; &quot;changeling,&quot; &quot;sasquatch,&quot; &quot;moth-creature,&quot; etc.<br /> - Power: The Beast may search for a creature whose Supernatural Tolerance trait is significantly lower than their Lair, about the same, or significantly higher.<br /> - Satiety: The Beast may search for a creature who is well-fed (70% of their resource pool or more), starving (30% of their resource pool or less), or neither.<br /> - Family: The Beast may search for specific Families, rather than simply looking for &quot;Beasts.&quot;<br /> <br /> On an Exceptional Success, the Beast may scent out even creatures on other planes of existence, and achieves Exceptional Success with 3 Successes on any roll for Primordial Pathways or Skeleton Key made to seek the creature out. Additionally, she gains access to the following criteria:<br /> <br /> - World: The Beast may search only a particular dimension of existence, such as &quot;the Shadow,&quot; &quot;Hedge,&quot; etc.<br /> - Talent: The Beast may search for a creature by their best supernatural talent, such as &quot;good at mind control,&quot; &quot;extremely hard to injure,&quot; and so on.<br /> - Hunger: The Beast may search for a Nemesis, a Tyrant or any of the other Hungers. If searching for a non-Beast, apply an equivalent trait (e.g. a Vampire who drinks blood from criminals, a Mage with an Obsession for the Astral).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-06-2020, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T13:24:21-07:00","id":1380753,"title":"","content":"<u><i><b>The Worst Thing In The World (\u2022 To \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></i></u><br /> When you inflict a Nightmare upon someone suffering from a Persistent Condition based on fear, you may increase your effective Satiety by [Merit Rating] and spend Willpower instead of Satiety. The latter effect is considered a variant of Lair Resonance, and thus consumes one of your [Lair] slots this scene. The Nightmare and the Persistent Condition must be symbolically related. For example: someone with a Persistent version of Frightened toward spiders would be a valid target for Bugs Everywhere.<br /> <br /> With the 2 dot version of this Merit, individuals suffering from non-Persistent Conditions are also valid targets, but the symbolic link must still be significant. With 3 dots in this Merit, the Beast no longer needs to target someone with a symbolically fitting Condition. However, if the target is suffering from such a Condition regardless, the Nightmare receives 9 Again. If the Condition is Persistent, the Nightmare receives 8 Again. If the Nightmare already has 8 Again for some reason (e.g. the High Satiety Effect of Behold My True Form), then the Beast benefits from Rote Quality instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-06-2020, 01:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T20:43:30-07:00","id":1384996,"title":"","content":"A Chamber of Your Own \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> Prerequisite: human<br /> Effect: you have a chamber all your own in the Primordial Dream. Cannot be taken over by an Insatiable as it's just a single Chamber all by itself, &amp; Insatiables need Lairs. Can be incorporated into a Hive with no ill effects. There are a couple (?) of Lair Traits attached to it, with all the normal applications of Lair Traits.<br /> Drawback: vulnerable to anathema. The Chamber does need to be fed (choose an emotion {fear, anger, sadness, joy, etc.} you use this emotion to feed your Chamber). The Chamber can be assimilated into the Lair of a Begotten who knows what they're doing, however this does have negative repercussions for you.<br /> <br /> Weird Hunger \u25cf<br /> Prerequisite: Begotten<br /> Effect: feeds off some emotion other than fear. Examples: anger, sadness, joy, awe, hate, anxiety, disgust, interest, nostalgia, etc.<br /> Drawback: makes it harder to communicate with other Begotten. Plus, a Begotten's capabilities are geared towards creating fear, first &amp; foremost. Your different hunger makes it harder to feed your satiety.<br /> <br /> Astral Roots \u25cf\u25cf<br /> Prerequisite: Begotten<br /> Effect: whatever Astral realm that you possessed before your Devouring did not collapse upon your Devouring. It is linked to your Lair via a small doorway in one of the Chambers in your Lair.<br /> Drawback: the link between your Lair &amp; your Astral realm goes both ways, &amp; you are not the only one who can use it. Anyone capable of getting into one of these two spaces &amp; finding the door to the other can get into the other one. Also, your ability to perceive what's happening at either door is rather fuzzy, meaning this is very much a blind spot.<br /> <br /> Ritemaster \u25cf\u25cf<br /> Prerequisites: Begotten; Obascus Rites<br /> Effect: You have successfully performed an Obascus Rite multiple times &amp; gained a deeper understanding of the rite in question. You gain a permanent +1 modifier for performing this Obascus Rite.<br /> Special: You can take this Merit multiple times, amping up the ease with which you can use one specific rite, or adding it to a different rite each time.<br /> <br /> Not sure about the costs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","user":"Krat05","date":"on Ritemaster to modifier. 06-18-2020, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T01:22:49-07:00","id":1385028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1384996#post1384996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Chamber of Your Own \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> Prerequisite: human<br /> Effect: you have a chamber all your own in the Primordial Dream. Cannot be taken over by an Insatiable as it's just a single Chamber all by itself, &amp; Insatiables need Lairs. Can be incorporated into a Hive with no ill effects. There are a couple (?) of Lair Traits attached to it, with all the normal applications of Lair Traits.<br /> Drawback: vulnerable to anathema. The Chamber does need to be fed (choose an emotion {fear, anger, sadness, joy, etc.} you use this emotion to feed your Chamber). The Chamber can be assimilated into the Lair of a Begotten who knows what they're doing, however this does have negative repercussions for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot understand how it's vulnerable to Anathema mechanics - can you more clearly describe it to me?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1384996#post1384996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird Hunger \u25cf<br /> Prerequisite: Begotten<br /> Effect: feeds off some emotion other than fear. Examples: anger, sadness, joy, awe, hate, anxiety, disgust, interest, nostalgia, etc.<br /> Drawback: makes it harder to communicate with other Begotten. Plus, a Begotten's capabilities are geared towards creating fear, first &amp; foremost. Your different hunger makes it harder to feed your satiety.</div> </div> </div> </div>HOW it's reflected mechaniclly? Some minuses to normal Feeding rolls? What are the rules for it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits?p=1384996#post1384996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ritemaster \u25cf\u25cf<br /> Prerequisites: Begotten; Obascus Rites<br /> Effect: You have successfully performed an Obascus Rite multiple times &amp; gained a deeper understanding of the rite in question. You automatically have better skill at performing this rite.<br /> Special: You can take this Merit multiple times, amping up the ease with which you can use one specific rite, or adding it to a different rite each time.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does 'You automatically have better skill at performing this rite' exactly mean? You get Exceptional Success on 3 dices instead of 5? What are <b>mechanics</b> of those Merits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T02:10:56-07:00","id":1385041,"title":"","content":"I have an easier time coming up with ideas than doing the mechanics. That said, these are good questions to ask.<br /> <br /> Weird Hunger: when I initially made this Merit I think I was thinking about it more as a story element than in the mechanics sense. For how it's reflected mechanically, perhaps you get less satiety from each feeding. A half, a third, two dots less satiety from each feeding?<br /> <br /> A Chamber of Your Own: vulnerable to anathema. What this means (I really should have made sure that I clarified this in the write-up of the Merit) is that anathema can be placed upon them as if they were Begotten. How the anathema work once placed? Well I remember reading that anathema impact a Begotten's healing factor, this Merit does not come with a healing factor &amp; does not assume there's a healing factor in the character, so we can't use that. How about ramping up the damage inflicted, to lethal if it wouldn't be otherwise, &amp; by adding some more dice if it is automatically lethal?<br /> <br /> Ritemaster: thinking about it, I feel like should shave a necessary die for every time this Merit is bought, but I'm not so sure that would work. Exceptional Success on 3 dices instead of 5 sounds like it could work, but it's not exactly what I was thinking of. When I made this Merit I was aiming for something that made it harder to fail at an Obcasus Rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T22:50:02-07:00","id":1401278,"title":"","content":"<u><i><b>Dark Walker Style (\u2022 To \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) [Original Concept By Deionscribe]</b></i></u><br /> Prerequisites: Beast<br /> <br /> (\u2022): Add [Style Rating] to rolls for Primordial Pathways and Skeleton Key.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022): The Beast has 8 Again for Primordial Pathways, or Rote Quality if he is in a location with Lair Resonance. For Skeleton Key, he has 8 Again as well, or Rote Quality if he has Family Ties with a supernatural entity linked to the otherworldly realm beyond the gateway.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022): The Beast no longer needs to spend a point of Willpower for rolls involving Primordial Pathways and Skeleton Key. However, he may spend it anyway to make the roll become reflexive in the case of Primordial Pathways. For Skeleton Key, this allows the gateway to remain open for hours equal to Successes rather than turns, and the Beast may reflexively close and reopen it during this time.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): When achieving an Exceptional Success to open a Primordial Pathway, the Beast can reflexively change its starting and end points during the scene, allowing him to freely explore the Primordial Dream and the otherworldly realms connected to it. When achieving an Exceptional Success to use Skeleton Key, he can add that gateway to a list with a maximum number of [Style Rating + Occult]. Whenever two gateways are part of this list, the Beast can enter one and emerge out of the other regardless of intervening distance. The gateways in this list may be redefined at the start of each Chapter.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): Whenever travelling through the Primordial Dream and the otherworldly realms connected to it as part of a Feeding, the Beast may spend 1 Willpower to forego the usual roll for Satiety Potential and score automatic Successes equal to his [Occult].<br /> <br /> <u><i><b>Gigantic Stride (Style, \u2022 To \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></i></u><br /> Prerequisites: Beast, Looming Presence Atavism, Sealed Exits Lair Trait, Intimidation \u2022\u2022\u2022, Family Ties With A Monster Who Is Very Hard To Escape From, Lair Equal To Merit Rating<br /> <br /> (\u2022): Decrease your effective Satiety by [Style Rating] for the purposes of Looming Presence.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022): Whenever your character participates in a Chase and his effective Satiety is Low for Looming Presence, he gains a bonus equal to Intimidation and Rote Quality.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022): Whenever your character spends Satiety for Looming Presence, make a reflexive roll of Presence + Intimidation + Lair. Instead of gaining +10 Speed, you multiply your Speed by [Highest Between Successes And Lair] + 1. Also, for the rest of the scene, any supernatural attempt to escape from you triggers a Clash Of Wills. Lastly, if you are inside the Lair or otherwise merged with your Horror and take advantage of how inescapable you are for Feeding your Hunger, you can forego the usual roll of Satiety Potential in order to score automatic Successes equal to [Intimidation].<br /> <br /> <u><i><b>Tenfold Armored Hide (Style, \u2022 To \u2022\u2022\u2022) </b></i></u><br /> Prerequisites: Beast, Stamina \u2022\u2022\u2022, Unbreakable Atavism, Exposed Lair Trait, Family Ties With A Monster Who Is Hard To Kill, Lair Equal To Merit Rating<br /> <br /> (\u2022): Decrease your effective Satiety by [Style Rating] for the purposes of Unbreakable.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022): Whenever your Beast's effective Satiety is Low for Unbreakable, any close quarters combat roll made against him which is reduced to zero damage suffers an additional negative effect based on the Skill. Brawl rolls inflict 1 Lethal Damage on the opponent. Weaponry rolls inflict [Stamina] in Structure Damage to the weapon that bypasses Durability.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022): Whenever the Beast spends Satiety for Unbreakable, he increases his Armor by 1/1 for each dot of Stamina during this scene. Anyone who makes an attack against the Beast as described in the previous Maneuver must make a reflexive roll of [Resolve + Composure] vs the Beast's [Stamina + Intimidation] or suffer the Frightened Condition.<br /> <br /> <u><i><b>Nightmarish Legions (Style, \u2022 To \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></i></u><br /> Prerequisites: Beast, Terror's Friend Atavism, Thralls Lair Trait, Intimidation \u2022\u2022\u2022, Family Ties With A Monster Who Commands Or Summons Thrall-Like Entities, Lair Equal To Merit Rating<br /> <br /> (\u2022): Decrease your effective Satiety by [Style Rating] for the purposes of Terror's Friend.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022): Whenever your character enters combat and his effective Satiety is Low for Terror's Friend, he can impose the Thralls Lair Trait without spending 1 Willpower, once per scene. He foregoes the usual roll, but scores 1 automatic Success. He also adds Intimidation to his Resolve for determining how many turns the Primordial Pathway lasts. Lastly, non-Thrall allies gain bonus dice equal to the Beast's [Intimidation], rather than just +2.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022): By spending Satiety for Terror's Friend, the character has Thralls equal to his entire [Lair] for the rest of the scene. Furthermore, his Thralls have an effective Skill for all rolls to protect and obey the Beast equal to his [Intimidation], and can mimic an additional Atavism. Lastly, any supernatural attempts to control his Thralls and other allies must contend with a Clash Of Wills, which gains a bonus equal to [Intimidation].<br /> <br /> <u><i><b>Mountains Of Ashes (Style, \u2022 To \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></i></u><br /> Prerequisites: Beast, Dragonfire Atavism, Burning Lair Trait, Athletics \u2022\u2022\u2022, Family Ties With A Monster Who Controls Fire, Lair Equal To Merit Rating<br /> <br /> (\u2022): Decrease your effective Satiety by [Style Rating] for the purposes of Dragonfire.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022): Whenever your character's effective Satiety is Low for Dragonfire, he is considered to have Influence (Fire 3). No roll is involved: the Beast scores automatic Successes equal to [Athletics] while unopposed, but is limited to a radius of [Horror's Finesse X 2] in meters. Mundane attempts to outmaneuver, remove and navigate through the ensuing Environmental Tilts suffer a penalty equal to [Athletics]. Supernatural attempts trigger a Clash Of Wills.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022): Whenever your character spends Satiety for Dragonfire, the normal Ranges are replaced by a flat maximum Range of [Horror's Finesse X 10] meters, which does not inflict dice penalties and stacks with Influence (Fire 3). This lasts for the scene. Furthermore, attacking with Dragonfire now benefits from Rote Quality during this turn. Lastly, if you are inside the Lair or otherwise merged with your Horror and take advantage of the flames for Feeding your Hunger, you can forego the usual roll of Satiety Potential in order to score automatic Successes equal to [Athletics].<br /> <br /> <u><i><b>Magnificent Hoard (\u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022, Style)</b></i></u><br /> Prerequisites: Beast, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1106128#post1106128\"><b>All That Glitters Atavism</b></a>, Hoard Lair Trait, Persuasion \u2022\u2022\u2022, Lair Equal To Merit Rating<br /> <br /> The stories are blooming with imagery of the dragon, reclining on his mound of gold coin; of the sirens tending to lost temples, replete with sunken copper; of modern plutocrats smothering their underlings through the stifling power of green paper, silver, and electricity. Wealth is resonant with the Begotten, and a lot of them learn to manipulate it in mystical ways.<br /> <br /> (\u2022): The Beast has Advanced Direction Sense for items represented by the Hoard Trait, even after they are brought into the real world. Resisting the urge to steal from his Hoard requires a roll of Resolve + Composure - the Beast's Persuasion during each hour that the trespassers remain within the Lair. The Beast lowers his effective Satiety for All That Glitters by [Style Rating]. Supernatural attempts to surreptitiously remove items from the Hoard trigger a Clash Of Wills.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022): When the Beast's effective Satiety is Low for All That Glitters, he can roll Manipulation + Persuasion + Lair to reshape and transmute items of his Hoard into any mundane Resources and Equipment he can imagine. Each Success creates one instance of such valuables, with a Cash Rating or Equipment Bonus equal to [Persuasion]. These valuables last for a number of days equal to [Lair] inside the real world, rather than hours. This can be used as Soft Leverage in Social Maneuvering.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022): Once per Chapter, when using the Second Maneuver, the Beast can make such valuables become fully real and thus last indefinitely outside the Lair by spending 1 Satiety. He can open a Primordial Pathway to any location containing items from his Hoard regardless of intervening distance, with a bonus to the roll equal to his Persuasion. If using such Primordial Pathways in order to Feed his Hunger, he can forego the usual roll for Satiety Potential and score automatic Successes equal to [Persuasion].<br /> <br /> <u><i><b>Eyes In The Dark (Style, \u2022 To \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></i></u><br /> Prerequisites: Beast, Survival \u2022\u2022\u2022, Needs Must Atavism, Mirages Lair Trait, Family Ties With A Monster Who Can Pierce Mystical Illusions And Falsehoods, Lair Equal To Merit Rating<br /> <br /> (\u2022): Decrease your effective Satiety by [Style Rating] for the purposes of Needs Must.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022): Whenever your Beast's effective Satiety is Low for Needs Must, she does not need to mark a target which is visible and within her immediate vicinity. She can mark any target which could raise her Satiety within a radius of [Horror's Finesse X 10] meters. If there is a Clash Of Wills involved, the Beast gains a bonus equal to [Survival]. The Beast can have a more specific notion of how and why the target might increase her Satiety with a reflexive roll of Wits + Survival + Lair, with Rote Quality.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022): Whenever the Beast spends Satiety for Needs Must, she is not limited to borrowing the senses of a living target for [Lair] minutes per day. The Beast adds the target to a list with a maximum number equal to [Horror's Finesse + Survival]. She can borrow the senses of such targets indefinitely and return to her own perceptions at will. Once per scene, the Beast can inflict the Mirages Lair Trait around the target, and has exact control over what they will perceive.<br /> <br /> The penalty for identifying illusions is increased to -5, and if the target has a supernatural ability to pierce illusions, they must succeed on a Clash Of Wills against the Beast, who gains a bonus equal to [Survival]. The Beast must still spend 1 Willpower, but foregoes the usual roll in order to score an automatic Success and adds Survival to his Resolve for determining how many turns the Primordial Pathway lasts. If taking advantage of these remotely controlled illusions to Feed his Hunger, the Beast can forego the usual roll for Satiety Potential to score automatic Successes equal to [Survival].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-25-2020, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-17T20:38:45-08:00","id":1435812,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Beast: Justification (1-3), You have worked out a reason and a philosophical justification that you use to look yourself in the mirror, whenever you feed according to your justification, gain a wp.</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26513-laguz-24","name":"Laguz 24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26513_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T12:33:49-07:00","id":1443154,"title":"","content":"Because the Player's Guide didn't give me enough mage-kinship merits. <b><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Ensorcelled Horror (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite</b>: Family Ties with a mage<br /> <b>Effect</b>: Your Horror has accepted the sorcery of your kin as part of its own Legend. You may carry a number spells as though you were a Sleepwalker, up to a maximum of your dots in this merit. You may only carry spells for mages with whom you have Family Ties.<br /> <br /> <b>Waking Nightmares (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite</b>: Family Ties with a mage<br /> <b>Effect</b>: The Primordial Dream resonates with the supernatural, rippling and shifting subtly in response to occult manifestations. Your character is highly attuned to the Dream, able to peer into its depths and discover mysteries normally hidden to the Begotten.<br /> You instinctively detect the slight tremors created by supernatural activity in the Dream, alerting you to the presence of any active, unconcealed supernatural phenomenon in range of your senses. In most cases, this functions identically to a mage\u2019s Peripheral Mage Sight (see Mage: The Awakening pg 90), though it does not actually count as Mage Sight for mechanics that specifically affect it (such as certain Prime spells). The Primordial Dream serves as a sufficient lens to detect the presence of supernatural activity, but you still lack a direct connection to the Supernal.<br /> Additionally, in a rough parody of a mage's Active Mage Sight, your character can gaze into the Primordial Dream in order to more closely perceive supernatural phenomena. By spending a point of a point of Willpower, you may extend your senses into the Primordial Dream as a reflexive action. In addition to revealing what would be apparent from simply seeing into the Dream (such as whether or not your current location is a Chamber), you can determine the location of any supernatural phenomenon within the range of your senses. This also allows you to detect phenomena concealed by supernatural means with a successful Clash of Wills. This ability lasts for a scene, and applies a -2 penalty to all mundane actions, unless it is ended early as a reflexive action.<br /> In a manner similar to the Family Resemblance Kinship ability, you may gain insight into the nature of any phenomenon whose reflection you perceive in the Primordial Dream (if the phenomenon turns out to be a creature, use Family Resemblance instead).<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: Wits + Occult + Lair \u2013 Opacity*<br /> <b>Action</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure</b>: The Beast\u2019s scrutiny provokes a nascent hunger in the nightmarish reflection of the target phenomenon, causing her to lose a point of Satiety and gain the Spooked Condition.<br /> <b>Failure</b>: The Beast learns nothing about this particular phenomenon.<br /> <b>Success</b>: The Beast is aware of the general nature of the phenomenon (such as \u201cstarts fires,\u201d \u201ccauses ill-fortune,\u201d \u201creveals thoughts,\u201d etc), as well as its approximate power level (expressed as a dot rating, if one exists, or the Supernal Potency of the effect\u2019s creator). If a supernatural creature is responsible for the phenomenon, the Beast learns the type of creature involved, as with Family Resemblance. If no creature was responsible, then the Beast may still get a sense for the metaphysical origin of the phenomenon. For example, if it originates in the Astral Realms, the Shadow, the machinations of the God Machine, etc.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: As above, plus the Beast instinctively knows the purpose for which the phenomenon was created (if any). She also receives a brief vision of the circumstances under which the phenomenon was created, including the specific creature responsible (if any).<br /> <br /> *Determine Opacity as you would for Focused Mage Sight (see Mage: The Awakening pg. 93), except you should increase the opacity of any phenomenon not related to the Primordial Dream (instead of the Supernal) by roughly 1.5 times. If the phenomenon is tied to the God Machine, instead triple the Opacity. As a quick rule of thumb, use the dot rating of the phenomenon, or half the Supernatural Potency of the creator (rounded up), as the base Opacity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":23730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","user":"Scriptorian","date":". 04-08-2021, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T00:32:44-07:00","id":1451024,"title":"","content":"<br /> I like that concept of special combinations giving a certain effect a lot. Kind of reminds me of the Isekai RPG Mechanics animes with secret skills. Sadly, I don't think these are as coherent as they could be. Maybe you could take a look, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a>? Feedback greatly appreciated!<br /> <br /> <u><i><b>Consume (Syle, \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></i></u><br /> Prerequisites: Beast, Stamina \u2022\u2022\u2022, Ravenous Maw Atavism, Hunting Ground Lair Trait, Family Ties With A Monster Who Heals Through Eating, Lair Equal To Merit Rating<br /> <br /> (\u2022): Decrease your effective Satiety by [Style Rating] for the purposes of Ravenous Maw.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022): Whenever your Beast's effective Satiety is Low for Ravenous Maw and they initiate a grapple, they can impose the Hunting Ground Lair Trait without spending 1 Willpower, once per scene. The Beast foregoes the usual roll, but scores 1 automatic Success. In addition, the Beast may choose to spent a WP to additionally open up another part of their body (e.g. the palms of their hands), which they can use to Damage during grapple as a 0L weapon.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022): Whenever the Beast spends Satiety for Ravenous Maw, they can heal Lethal Damage up to an amount equal to 1/2 the size of a living creature they swallow. Anyone targeted by an attack as described in the previous Maneuver must make a reflexive roll of [Resolve + Composure] vs the Beast's [Strength + Intimidation] or suffer the Frightened Condition.<br /> <br /> (Was trying to go for the feeling of a Monster using their victims' Biomass to heal, like Alex Mercer or Carrion or the Thing.)<br /> <br /> <u><i><b>Made of Death (Syle, \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></i></u><br /> Prerequisites: Beast, Stamina \u2022\u2022\u2022, Skin Deep Atavism, Razored Lair Trait OR Corrosive Lair Trait, Family Ties With A Monster Who Is Harmful To Touch, Lair Equal To Merit Rating<br /> <br /> (\u2022): Decrease your effective Satiety by [Style Rating] for the purposes of Skin Deep.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022): Whenever your Beast's effective Satiety is Low for Skin Deep, he gains an additional Modification that can be exclusively used to either grow spikes, thorns, blades or similar objects protruding from their body or be dripping with corrosive substances covering their whole body (depending on the prerequisite Lair Trait). Physical contact with the Beast deals an automatic 1/2 [Lair] Bashing Damage per turn, rounded down.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022): Whenever the Beast spends Satiety for Skin Deep, he can spend 1 WP to shoot out their blades or acid to cover an area equal to [Lair x 3] yards around them in it, dealing [Lair] Bashing damage to everyone in it and inflicting the Razored/Corrosive Tilt on the area but losing the (\u2022\u2022) Bonus Modification. Defense does not apply to this attack, though armor does, and characters may attempt to Dodge this attack. This works once per scene.<br /> <br /> (Probably Anime-inspired, but I keep thinking of Lavos from Chrono Trigger)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><i><u>Storage (\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</u></i></b><br /> With this Merit, a Beast is capable of storing Satiety up to half their dots in this merit in their Lair for later consumption. Stored Satiety deteriorates quickly, at a rate of 1 per day, and can be destroyed by intruders. Stored Satiety takes on an appearance based on the Beast's Hunger and Horror (maybe a large sack of biomass for a Predator, a collection of whispers or a Skyrim-like Thu'um wall for a Whisper, a glowing precious ring for an Hoarder etc.). Should the Satiety leave the Lair, or the Chamber be disconnected from the Lair for some reason (e.g. collapsing), it dissolves into putrid ectoplasma.<br /> Consuming another Beast's Satiety does not fulfill one's own Hunger, but can be used to satisfy Horror Spawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 06-05-2021, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}